{"drafts":[{"assumptions":["ASM-13 (basket stored per user on the server) and ASM-29 (basket kept for the browser session only) conflict. REQ-26 follows ASM-13 because it is the stronger version of the request's 'persist if the customer navigates away'. This needs confirming.","ASM-12 and ASM-32 do not actually answer whether a locked-out user can reset their password. The spec leaves this open (see suggestions).","Product prices and order totals are net and in a single currency with 2 decimal places. Invoice tax is calculated on the net total and rounded half-up to 2 decimals (Q-4).","The ERP stock CSV has a distributor product code column and a quantity column. Rows are matched to products on distributor product code.","One malformed row makes the whole stock file invalid, so partial data never replaces good data. A scheduled run that finds no file is recorded as Failed.","A product that has never appeared in a stock import has quantity 0 (Out of stock). A product missing from a later file keeps its previous quantity.","The low-stock threshold includes its boundary: a quantity equal to the threshold counts as Low stock.","Basket and order quantities are counted in the product's unit of sale.","Order emails go to the buyer who placed the order. For orders staff create, they go to the customer company's contact email.","No management role exists. Reports and the dashboard are available to office staff and administrators. Sales figures count only Delivered orders, at net prices.","Product images must be JPEG, PNG or WebP and at most 5 MB. These limits are placeholders until dimensions and storage are decided.","The order note is limited to 1000 characters.","Distributor product codes and customer account numbers are unique.","A deactivated price list cannot be newly assigned. Customers still assigned to it see its products as having no price until they are given a new list.","Staff quantity edits are not checked against stock when they are made. The check runs at confirmation. Staff cannot remove an order's last line and must reject the order instead.","When an order is repeated, any quantity above current stock is reduced to the available quantity and flagged (ASM-7).","The invoice date is the date, in the business timezone, when the order became Delivered. A payment date cannot be later than today.","Fuel type is part of each vehicle compatibility record so that vehicle search can filter on it.","The first administrator account comes from seed data at set-up (ASM-16).","The performance, retention, session and availability figures in the NFRs are proposals and need sign-off."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 ≤ 1 s with 50,000 active products and 100 concurrent users","text":"Catalogue search and category/vehicle filtering response time"},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"p95 ≤ 2 s for baskets of up to 100 lines","text":"Checkout review and order submission response time"},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"A 100,000-row CSV is fully validated and applied within 10 minutes","text":"Nightly stock import duration"},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"p95 ≤ 3 s for invoices of up to 200 lines","text":"Invoice PDF generation time"},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"100% of passwords stored with Argon2id or bcrypt (cost ≥ 12); 0 plaintext or reversible passwords","text":"Password storage"},{"id":"NFR-6","metric":"100% of endpoints served over TLS 1.2 or higher; plain HTTP redirected or refused","text":"Transport security for all portal traffic, including PII and invoice data"},{"id":"NFR-7","metric":"Sessions expire after 30 minutes without activity","text":"Idle session expiry"},{"id":"NFR-8","metric":"0 records of another company returned across an automated authorisation test suite covering 100% of customer endpoints","text":"Company data isolation"},{"id":"NFR-9","metric":"Kept for at least 7 years; 0 records deleted when a user or company is deactivated","text":"Retention of orders, invoices, timelines and audit log entries"},{"id":"NFR-10","metric":"≥ 99.5% monthly uptime, excluding announced maintenance windows","text":"Availability of the portal"},{"id":"NFR-11","metric":"Conforms to WCAG 2.1 level AA, with 0 critical issues in an automated accessibility scan","text":"Accessibility of customer-facing screens"}],"outOfScope":["Customer Account Manager role (Q-1)","Customers creating or editing their own delivery addresses (Q-3)","Saved basket templates, including sharing them (ASM-1, ASM-20)","Backorders and ordering more than the imported stock quantity (ASM-7; request section 8)","Stock reservation or reducing portal stock when orders are placed (ASM-22)","Writing stock or any other data back to the ERP (request section 9)","Online card payments and payment methods (request section 32)","Route planning (request section 22)","Social login or single sign-on (ASM-12)","SMS or push notifications; editable email templates (ASM-14, ASM-21)","Migrating existing customers, products, prices or past orders (ASM-16)","Nested categories (ASM-10, ASM-33)","Separate Rejected order status (ASM-9, ASM-28)","Importing vehicle compatibility data in bulk from an external source (ASM-15, ASM-34)","Custom report builder (ASM-2, ASM-31)","Volume pricing, promotional pricing, discounts and price effective dates (request section 10)","Reproducing an existing client invoice template"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active customer buyer of an active company with password 'Correct#Pass1'","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 200 with a session, and a following request to the buyer's order history with that session returns 200","when":"POST sign-in with that email and password"},{"given":"An active user account","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"Both responses are 401 with the same message 'Invalid email or password' and no session is created","when":"POST sign-in with the right email and a wrong password, and separately with an email that is not registered"},{"given":"No session","id":"AC-1.3","level":"api","then":"Response is 401","when":"A customer, staff or administrator endpoint is called"}],"ears":"When a user submits an email address and password that match an active account, the portal shall start an authenticated session for that user.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in buyer with session S","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"The call returns 401","when":"The buyer signs out and then calls the order history endpoint with session S"}],"ears":"When a signed-in user signs out, the portal shall invalidate that user's session.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active account with 5 consecutive failed sign-ins, the last at 10:00","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"Sign-in is refused with a message that the account is temporarily locked and no session is created","when":"The correct password is submitted at 10:10"},{"given":"The same locked account","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"Sign-in succeeds","when":"The correct password is submitted at 10:15 or later"},{"given":"An account with 4 consecutive failed sign-ins","id":"AC-3.3","level":"api","then":"Both correct sign-ins succeed because a successful sign-in resets the failure count","when":"The correct password is submitted, then 4 more wrong passwords, then the correct password"}],"ears":"If a user account has 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, then the portal shall lock that account for 15 minutes from the fifth failed attempt.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A registered active user","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The email service receives one message to that address containing a reset link","when":"A password reset is requested for that email"},{"given":"A reset link issued 30 minutes ago","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"Sign-in with the new password succeeds, sign-in with the old password returns 401, and a second use of the same link is rejected","when":"The user sets a new password through the link"},{"given":"A reset link issued 61 minutes ago with the default expiry","id":"AC-4.3","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected as expired and the password is unchanged","when":"The user submits a new password through the link"},{"given":"An email address that is not registered","id":"AC-4.4","level":"api","then":"The response is the same as for a registered address and the email service receives no message","when":"A password reset is requested"}],"ears":"When a user requests a password reset for a registered email address, the portal shall email a single-use reset link that expires after the configured reset expiry (default 1 hour).","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-11","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An administrator","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"The email service receives an invitation message to that address and the user is listed with status Invited","when":"The administrator invites buyer 'ann@workshop-a.test' linked to company Workshop A"},{"given":"An invited user whose link is 2 days old","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"The user status is Active and sign-in succeeds","when":"The user sets a password through the link and then signs in"},{"given":"An invitation link that is 8 days old","id":"AC-5.3","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected as expired and the user stays Invited","when":"The invitee opens it to set a password"},{"given":"An administrator","id":"AC-5.4","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected with a validation error","when":"The administrator invites a customer buyer without a customer company"}],"ears":"When an administrator invites a customer buyer or an office staff user, the portal shall email an invitation link that expires after the configured invitation expiry (default 7 days) and activates the account once the invitee sets a password.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","ASM-11","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An invited user with link L1","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"Setting a password through L1 is rejected and through L2 succeeds","when":"The administrator resends the invitation, producing link L2"}],"ears":"When an administrator resends an invitation, the portal shall invalidate the previous invitation link for that user.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user deactivated by an administrator","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"Sign-in is refused and no session is created","when":"The user signs in with the correct password"},{"given":"A buyer with an open session whose account is then deactivated","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected with 401 or 403 and no order is created","when":"The buyer submits an order with that session"},{"given":"Customer company Fleet B set to inactive, with 3 past orders and 2 invoices","id":"AC-7.3","level":"api","then":"The buyer's sign-in is refused, and staff still see all 3 orders and 2 invoices","when":"A buyer of Fleet B signs in, and an office staff user lists Fleet B's orders and invoices"}],"ears":"If a deactivated user, or a user of an inactive customer company, attempts to sign in or to submit an order, then the portal shall reject the request.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer A1 of company A and order O-B of company B","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"Both requests return 404 and no data of company B is returned","when":"A1 requests O-B's detail and O-B's invoice PDF by id"},{"given":"Buyers A1 and A2 of company A, each with one order, and company B with one order","id":"AC-8.2","level":"api","then":"The list contains the orders of A1 and A2 and not company B's order","when":"A1 lists order history"},{"given":"Buyer A1","id":"AC-8.3","level":"api","then":"The requests return 404","when":"A1 requests the delivery addresses or account details of company B by id"}],"ears":"The portal shall limit each customer buyer's access to the orders, invoices, prices, delivery addresses and account details of the buyer's own company.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-9","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in customer buyer","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"Each call returns 403","when":"The buyer calls the staff order queue, the delivery list export and the product create endpoint"},{"given":"A signed-in office staff user","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"Each call returns 403","when":"The user calls product create, price list edit, user role change, system settings update and audit log view"}],"ears":"If a customer buyer calls an office staff or administrator function, or an office staff user calls an administrator-only function, then the portal shall reject the call with 403.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active products 'Brake Pad Set' (code BRK-1023, part no. 0986-494, brand Bosch) and 'Oil Filter' (code FLT-200)","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"Each search returns 'Brake Pad Set' and none returns 'Oil Filter'","when":"The buyer searches 'pad', 'BRK-10', '494' and 'bosch' in turn"},{"given":"A retired product 'Old Brake Disc'","id":"AC-10.2","level":"api","then":"The retired product is not returned","when":"The buyer searches 'brake disc'"}],"ears":"When a customer buyer searches the catalogue with a text term, the portal shall return active products whose product name, distributor product code, manufacturer part number or manufacturer/brand contains the term, ignoring letter case.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"3 active products in 'Filters' and 5 in 'Brake system'","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"The results are the 3 filter products, then the 5 brake products, then all 8 products","when":"The buyer filters by 'Filters', then changes to 'Brake system', then clears the filter"},{"given":"'Oil Filter' and 'Air Filter' in 'Filters' and 'Oil Pump' in 'Engine parts'","id":"AC-11.2","level":"api","then":"Only 'Oil Filter' is returned","when":"The buyer searches 'oil' with category 'Filters'"}],"ears":"When a customer buyer selects a category filter, the portal shall return only active products assigned to that category.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","ASM-10","ASM-33"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P1 compatible with VW Golf 2018 1.6 TDI Diesel and product P2 compatible with VW Golf 2018 1.4 TSI Petrol","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"Only P1 is returned","when":"The buyer searches make VW, model Golf, year 2018, fuel type Diesel"},{"given":"The same data","id":"AC-12.2","level":"api","then":"P1 and P2 are returned","when":"The buyer searches make VW, model Golf, year 2018"}],"ears":"When a customer buyer searches by vehicle using any combination of make, model, year, engine, fuel type and variant, the portal shall return active products that have a compatibility record matching every supplied attribute.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","ASM-15","ASM-34"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active product with image, unit 'each', pack size 4, price 42.00 on the buyer's price list and stock 0","id":"AC-13.1","level":"api","then":"The entry includes the image URL, name, code, manufacturer, unit 'each', pack size 4, price 42.00 and stock status 'Out of stock'","when":"The buyer lists the catalogue"}],"ears":"The portal shall return, for each catalogue list entry, the product image, product name, distributor product code, manufacturer, unit of sale, pack size, the buyer's price and the stock status.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active product with a description and 2 compatibility records","id":"AC-14.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains the list fields, the description and both compatibility records","when":"The buyer opens the product detail"},{"given":"An active product with imported quantity 0","id":"AC-14.2","level":"api","then":"The product is returned with stock status 'Out of stock'","when":"The buyer opens the product detail"}],"ears":"When a customer buyer opens a product detail, the portal shall return the catalogue list fields plus the description and the product's vehicle compatibility records.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P priced 42.00 on 'Workshop A' list (assigned to company A) and 50.00 on 'Standard' list (assigned to company B)","id":"AC-15.1","level":"api","then":"Buyer A sees 42.00 and buyer B sees 50.00","when":"A buyer of A and a buyer of B open P"},{"given":"The same data","id":"AC-15.2","level":"api","then":"Buyer A sees 50.00","when":"An administrator assigns 'Standard' to company A and buyer A opens P again"}],"ears":"The portal shall show each customer buyer the net price from the price list assigned to the buyer's company.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product P with stock 10 that is not on company A's price list","id":"AC-16.1","level":"api","then":"P is listed with a no-price marker and no amount, and the add request is rejected with a no-price error","when":"A buyer of A lists the catalogue and then adds 1 of P to the basket"}],"ears":"If a product has no price on the price list assigned to the buyer's company, then the portal shall show the product marked as having no price and reject adding it to the basket.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-7","ASM-3","I-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An administrator","id":"AC-17.1","level":"api","then":"A buyer of C sees P at 37.50","when":"The administrator creates list 'Fleet', sets P to 37.50, and assigns 'Fleet' to company C"},{"given":"'Fleet' assigned to company C with P at 37.50","id":"AC-17.2","level":"api","then":"A buyer of C sees P marked as having no price","when":"The administrator removes P from 'Fleet'"},{"given":"A deactivated price list 'Old Dealer'","id":"AC-17.3","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected with a validation error","when":"The administrator assigns it to a company"},{"given":"An administrator","id":"AC-17.4","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected with a validation error","when":"The administrator sets a price of 0 or -5"}],"ears":"Where a user has the administrator role, the portal shall let that user create, rename and deactivate price lists, set, edit and remove product prices on them, and assign one price list to each customer company.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Low-stock threshold 5","id":"AC-18.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns Out of stock, Low stock, Low stock and In stock","when":"The stock status classification is called with quantities 0, 1, 5 and 6"},{"given":"Low-stock threshold 5","id":"AC-18.2","level":"unit","then":"It returns Out of stock","when":"The classification is called for a product that has never had an imported quantity"}],"ears":"The portal shall classify a product's stock status as Out of stock when its imported quantity is 0, Low stock when it is from 1 up to and including the configured low-stock threshold, and In stock when it is above that threshold.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-12","ASM-4","ASM-24"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product BRK-1023 with quantity 3 and a valid file listing BRK-1023 with quantity 40 in the configured location","id":"AC-19.1","level":"job","then":"BRK-1023 shows quantity 40 and status In stock (threshold 5), and an import record shows Succeeded with run time and 1 row applied","when":"The import job runs"},{"given":"No file in the configured location","id":"AC-19.2","level":"job","then":"All stock quantities are unchanged and an import record shows Failed with reason 'no file found'","when":"The import job runs"}],"ears":"When the scheduled nightly stock import runs, the portal shall read the newest stock CSV from the configured folder or SFTP location and replace the stock quantities of the listed products with the file's quantities.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","ASM-6","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Current quantities from the last good import and a new file whose row 3 has quantity 'abc'","id":"AC-20.1","level":"job","then":"No product quantity changes and the import record shows Failed with a reason naming row 3","when":"The import job runs"},{"given":"A file with no quantity column","id":"AC-20.2","level":"job","then":"No product quantity changes and the import record shows Failed with reason 'missing quantity column'","when":"The import job runs"}],"ears":"If the stock file is unreadable or empty, lacks the product identifier or quantity column, or has any quantity that is not a whole number of 0 or more, then the portal shall keep all previous stock quantities and record the import as Failed with the reason.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A valid file with rows BRK-1023=40 and XYZ-999=7, where XYZ-999 is unknown","id":"AC-21.1","level":"job","then":"BRK-1023 shows 40, and the import record shows Succeeded with warnings listing XYZ-999","when":"The import job runs"}],"ears":"If an otherwise valid stock file contains product identifiers not known to the portal, then the portal shall apply the rows for known products, skip the unknown rows, and record the import as Succeeded with warnings listing the skipped identifiers.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","ASM-5","ASM-26"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"One Succeeded, one Succeeded-with-warnings and one Failed import","id":"AC-22.1","level":"api","then":"All 3 are listed newest first with run time, outcome, rows applied, and the failure reason or skipped identifiers","when":"An office staff user lists stock imports"}],"ears":"The portal shall show office staff and administrators a list of stock imports with run time, outcome, rows applied, and the failure reason or skipped identifiers.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Priced product P with imported quantity 8","id":"AC-23.1","level":"api","then":"The basket has one line for P with quantity 8","when":"The buyer adds 8 of P"},{"given":"The same product P","id":"AC-23.2","level":"api","then":"Both requests are rejected; the 9 request states 8 available; the line stays at 8","when":"The buyer sets the quantity to 9, then to 0"},{"given":"Priced product Q with imported quantity 0","id":"AC-23.3","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected as out of stock","when":"The buyer adds 1 of Q"},{"given":"A basket line of 3 for P (stock 8)","id":"AC-23.4","level":"api","then":"The basket still has one line for P, now with quantity 5","when":"The buyer adds 2 more of P"}],"ears":"When a customer buyer adds a product to the basket or changes a basket line quantity, the portal shall accept only whole quantities from 1 up to the product's latest imported stock quantity.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-7","ASM-22"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket with lines P (2 × 10.00) and Q (1 × 5.00)","id":"AC-24.1","level":"api","then":"The basket has only line P and subtotal 20.00","when":"The buyer removes line Q"}],"ears":"When a customer buyer removes a basket line, the portal shall delete that line from the basket and recalculate the subtotal.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket with P (3 × 12.50) and Q (2 × 4.25)","id":"AC-25.1","level":"api","then":"Line totals are 37.50 and 8.50, the subtotal is 46.00, and the tax note is present","when":"The buyer views the basket"}],"ears":"The portal shall return the basket with each line's unit net price, line total of unit price times quantity, the net subtotal, and a note that tax is added on the invoice.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","Q-4","ASM-30"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer A1 with 2 basket lines","id":"AC-26.1","level":"api","then":"The basket has the same 2 lines and quantities","when":"A1 signs out and signs in with a new session"},{"given":"Buyers A1 and A2 of the same company, A1 with 2 basket lines","id":"AC-26.2","level":"api","then":"A2's basket does not contain A1's lines","when":"A2 views the basket"}],"ears":"The portal shall store each buyer's basket on the server per user, so that it is unchanged after the buyer signs out and signs in again on any device.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A with 2 active delivery addresses and 1 deactivated address","id":"AC-27.1","level":"api","then":"Only the 2 active addresses are returned","when":"A buyer of A requests the checkout address options"},{"given":"A buyer of company A","id":"AC-27.2","level":"api","then":"The selection is rejected, and the create call returns 403 or 404","when":"The buyer selects an address id belonging to company B, and separately calls a create-address endpoint"}],"ears":"When a customer buyer selects a delivery address at checkout, the portal shall accept only an active delivery address of the buyer's own company.","id":"REQ-27","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Cutoff 14:00, no holidays","id":"AC-28.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns Tuesday, Wednesday and Wednesday","when":"The earliest delivery date calculation is called for Monday 13:00, Monday 14:00 and Monday 15:00"},{"given":"Cutoff 14:00, no holidays","id":"AC-28.2","level":"unit","then":"It returns Monday, Tuesday and Monday","when":"Called for Friday 13:00, Friday 15:00 and Saturday 10:00"},{"given":"Cutoff 14:00 and Friday entered as a holiday","id":"AC-28.3","level":"unit","then":"It returns the following Monday","when":"Called for Thursday 13:00"},{"given":"Business timezone Europe/Berlin in summer time, cutoff 14:00","id":"AC-28.4","level":"unit","then":"It returns Wednesday","when":"Called for Monday 12:30 UTC (14:30 local)"}],"ears":"The portal shall calculate the earliest delivery date as the next working day for orders placed before the configured cutoff time (default 14:00) and as the second working day for orders placed at or after the cutoff, using the configured business timezone, where working days exclude Saturdays, Sundays and administrator-entered holiday dates.","id":"REQ-28","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-8","ASM-23"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order submitted Monday 15:00 with no holidays","id":"AC-29.1","level":"api","then":"Both submissions are rejected with a delivery-date error and no order is created","when":"The buyer submits with delivery date Tuesday, and separately with Saturday"},{"given":"An order submitted Monday 15:00","id":"AC-29.2","level":"api","then":"The order is created with delivery date Wednesday","when":"The buyer submits with delivery date Wednesday"}],"ears":"If a submitted delivery date is earlier than the earliest delivery date or falls on a non-working day, then the portal shall reject the order submission.","id":"REQ-29","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket line of 6 for P, after which a stock import sets P to 4","id":"AC-30.1","level":"api","then":"The submission is rejected naming P with 4 available, and no order is created","when":"The buyer submits the order"},{"given":"A basket line for Q, after which an administrator retires Q","id":"AC-30.2","level":"api","then":"The submission is rejected naming Q as unavailable","when":"The buyer submits the order"}],"ears":"If at order submission any line exceeds the product's latest imported stock quantity or the product is out of stock, retired or has no price, then the portal shall reject the submission and identify the affected lines.","id":"REQ-30","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-7","ASM-22"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A buyer who reviewed checkout with P at 42.00, after which an administrator changes P to 45.00","id":"AC-31.1","level":"api","then":"The submission is rejected with P's updated price 45.00 and no order is created","when":"The buyer submits the order"},{"given":"The same buyer","id":"AC-31.2","level":"api","then":"The order is created with P at 45.00","when":"The buyer requests the checkout review again and then submits"}],"ears":"If the current price of any basket line differs from the price the buyer last reviewed at checkout, then the portal shall reject the order submission and return the updated prices for the buyer to review again.","id":"REQ-31","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket with 2 lines, a selected address, delivery date and note, where one line exceeds current stock","id":"AC-32.1","level":"api","then":"The response holds both lines with prices, the net total, address, date, note, and a stock problem for the over-stock line","when":"The buyer requests the checkout review"}],"ears":"When a customer buyer requests the checkout review, the portal shall return the lines with current net prices and quantities, the net total, the selected delivery address and date, the note, and any stock or price problems.","id":"REQ-32","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A valid reviewed basket with 2 lines","id":"AC-33.1","level":"api","then":"An order with a new unique order number and status Received is returned, its timeline has one Received entry with the buyer and time, and the buyer's basket is empty","when":"The buyer submits"},{"given":"The order just created","id":"AC-33.2","level":"api","then":"The order is listed with status Received","when":"An office staff user opens the order queue"},{"given":"An order with P at 42.00","id":"AC-33.3","level":"api","then":"The order still shows P at 42.00","when":"An administrator changes P on the company's price list to 48.00 and the buyer reopens the order"},{"given":"A valid basket","id":"AC-33.4","level":"api","then":"The submission is rejected with a validation error","when":"The buyer submits with a note of 1001 characters"}],"ears":"When a customer buyer submits an order that passes all checkout checks, the portal shall create an order with a unique order number, status Received, the lines with their order-time net prices, the delivery address, the delivery date and the optional note.","id":"REQ-33","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-4","I-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Orders in Received, Picking and Delivered status","id":"AC-34.1","level":"api","then":"All three are rejected and the statuses are unchanged","when":"Office staff try Received→Picking, Picking→Cancelled and Delivered→Out for delivery"},{"given":"Orders in Confirmed and Picking status","id":"AC-34.2","level":"api","then":"Both changes succeed","when":"Office staff move Confirmed→Picking and Picking→Out for delivery"}],"ears":"The portal shall allow an order's status to change only one step forward along Received, Confirmed, Picking, Out for delivery, Delivered, or to Cancelled from Received or Confirmed.","id":"REQ-34","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-27"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order placed by buyer A1 and confirmed by staff user S1","id":"AC-35.1","level":"api","then":"The timeline shows Received (A1), Confirmed (S1) and Picking (S1), each with date and time, in order","when":"S1 moves it to Picking and the buyer opens the order"}],"ears":"When an order's status changes, the portal shall append a timeline entry with the new status, the date and time, and the user or system that made the change.","id":"REQ-35","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-5","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Orders from companies A and B in Received and Confirmed status over 3 days","id":"AC-36.1","level":"api","then":"Only A's Received orders placed in that range are returned with all listed fields","when":"Staff filter by customer A, status Received and a 1-day date range"}],"ears":"When office staff open the order queue, the portal shall list orders of all customers with order number, customer, order date, requested delivery date, net total and current status, filterable by customer, order-date range and status.","id":"REQ-36","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order with P quantity 10","id":"AC-37.1","level":"api","then":"The order shows P at 6 and its amendment history shows S1, the time, P quantity 10→6","when":"Staff user S1 changes P to 6"},{"given":"A Confirmed order","id":"AC-37.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected and the order is unchanged","when":"Staff change any line quantity"},{"given":"A Received order of company A placed Monday 15:00","id":"AC-37.3","level":"api","then":"Both requests are rejected","when":"Staff set delivery date Tuesday, or an address of company B"},{"given":"A Received order with a single line","id":"AC-37.4","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected; staff must reject the order instead","when":"Staff remove that line"}],"ears":"While an order is in Received status, the portal shall let office staff change line quantities, remove lines, change the delivery date and delivery address, and edit the note, recording each change with the staff user, time, field, previous value and new value.","id":"REQ-37","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order placed by buyer A1 with P quantity 10","id":"AC-38.1","level":"api","then":"The email service receives a message to A1 with the order number and 'P: 10 → 6'","when":"Staff change P to 6"}],"ears":"When office staff change a line quantity or remove a line on an order, the portal shall email the order's buyer the order number and each changed line's previous and new quantity.","id":"REQ-38","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-14","ASM-21"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order with P quantity 4 and P stock 10","id":"AC-39.1","level":"api","then":"The status is Confirmed with S1 and the time recorded, and a later buyer cancel request is rejected","when":"Staff user S1 confirms it"},{"given":"A Received order with P quantity 12 and P stock 10","id":"AC-39.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected naming P and the status stays Received","when":"Staff confirm it"},{"given":"A Received order of a company set to inactive","id":"AC-39.3","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected and the status stays Received","when":"Staff confirm it"}],"ears":"When office staff confirm a Received order whose line quantities are all within the latest imported stock and whose customer company is active, the portal shall set the status to Confirmed and record the confirming user and time.","id":"REQ-39","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order by buyer A1 where staff changed P from 10 to 6","id":"AC-40.1","level":"api","then":"The email service receives a message to A1 with the order number, lines, net total, delivery address and date, and 'P: 10 → 6'","when":"Staff confirm it"}],"ears":"When an order becomes Confirmed, the portal shall email the order's buyer the order number, lines with quantities and net prices, net total, delivery address and date, and any staff quantity changes.","id":"REQ-40","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-14","ASM-21"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Confirmed order by buyer A1","id":"AC-41.1","level":"api","then":"The status is Cancelled with reason, S1 and time on the timeline, and the email service receives a message to A1 with the order number and reason","when":"Staff user S1 rejects it with reason 'Part discontinued'"},{"given":"A Received order","id":"AC-41.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected and the status stays Received","when":"Staff reject it with an empty reason"}],"ears":"When office staff reject an order in Received or Confirmed status with a reason, the portal shall set the order to Cancelled, record the reason, rejecting user and time, and email the buyer the order number and reason.","id":"REQ-41","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-9","ASM-28","ASM-27"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Picking order by buyer A1","id":"AC-42.1","level":"api","then":"The email service receives a message to A1 with the order number stating it is out for delivery","when":"Staff move it to Out for delivery"}],"ears":"When an order's status changes to Out for delivery, the portal shall email the order's buyer the order number and a statement that the order is out for delivery.","id":"REQ-42","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A on a price list with P at 42.00, P stock 10","id":"AC-43.1","level":"api","then":"A Received order is created with P at 42.00 and 'created by S1 (staff)'","when":"Staff user S1 creates an order for A with 3 of P, an A address, a valid delivery date and a note"},{"given":"That order","id":"AC-43.2","level":"api","then":"The order is listed and its detail shows it was created by staff","when":"A buyer of company A lists order history"},{"given":"P stock 10","id":"AC-43.3","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected","when":"Staff create an order for A with 11 of P, or with a delivery date before the earliest date"}],"ears":"When office staff submit an order on behalf of a customer company, the portal shall create the order with that company's price list, delivery address, delivery-date and stock rules, and record it as created by that staff user.","id":"REQ-43","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Companies 'Workshop Alpha' (ACC-100) and 'Fleet Beta' (ACC-200)","id":"AC-44.1","level":"api","then":"The first returns Workshop Alpha and the second Fleet Beta, each with details, addresses and price list","when":"Staff search 'alpha', then 'ACC-2'"}],"ears":"When office staff search customers by company name or account number, the portal shall return matching customer companies with their details, delivery addresses and assigned price list.","id":"REQ-44","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"For 2026-11-03: 2 Confirmed orders, 1 Out for delivery order and 1 Cancelled order; 1 Confirmed order for 2026-11-04","id":"AC-45.1","level":"api","then":"The CSV has a header and 3 rows with all listed columns, excluding the Cancelled order and the 2026-11-04 order","when":"Staff export the delivery list for 2026-11-03"}],"ears":"When office staff export the delivery list for a date, the portal shall return a CSV with one row per non-cancelled order due for delivery on that date, holding order number, customer, delivery address, contact person and phone, delivery date, order lines as product code and quantity, note and status.","id":"REQ-45","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A with 3 orders by 2 buyers, including one staff-created","id":"AC-46.1","level":"api","then":"All 3 orders are listed with all listed fields","when":"Buyer A1 opens order history"}],"ears":"When a customer buyer opens order history, the portal shall list all orders of the buyer's company with order number, order date, delivery date, delivery address, net total and status.","id":"REQ-46","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Confirmed order where staff changed P from 10 to 6","id":"AC-47.1","level":"api","then":"All listed fields are returned, including the timeline and the amendment 'P: 10 → 6'","when":"The buyer opens it"},{"given":"An order containing product R that was retired afterwards","id":"AC-47.2","level":"api","then":"The line for R is shown with its order-time name, quantity and price","when":"The buyer opens it"}],"ears":"When a customer buyer opens an order of the buyer's company, the portal shall return the order number, order date, customer, delivery address, requested delivery date, current status, status timeline, lines with quantities, unit prices and line totals, order total, note and staff amendments.","id":"REQ-47","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order placed by buyer A2 of company A","id":"AC-48.1","level":"api","then":"The status is Cancelled and the timeline shows the cancellation by A1","when":"Buyer A1 of company A cancels it"},{"given":"A Confirmed order of company A","id":"AC-48.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected with a message to contact the distributor office and the status stays Confirmed","when":"Buyer A1 cancels it"}],"ears":"When an active customer buyer cancels an order of the buyer's company that is in Received status, the portal shall set the order to Cancelled with a timeline entry naming that buyer.","id":"REQ-48","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A past order by colleague A2 with P (qty 3, then 42.00, now 45.00, stock 10), R (retired) and Q (stock 0)","id":"AC-49.1","level":"api","then":"A1's basket gains P × 3 at 45.00, R and Q are returned as flagged and not added, and no new order is created","when":"Buyer A1 repeats it"},{"given":"A past order with P quantity 12 and P stock now 10","id":"AC-49.2","level":"api","then":"P is added with quantity 10 and flagged as reduced to available stock","when":"The buyer repeats it"}],"ears":"When an active customer buyer repeats an order of the buyer's company, the portal shall add each still-orderable product to the buyer's basket at the current price-list price and return flags for products that are retired, unpriced or out of stock without adding them.","id":"REQ-49","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Tax rate 20%, payment terms 30 days, an Out for delivery order with net total 100.00","id":"AC-50.1","level":"api","then":"One invoice exists with invoice date 2026-11-03, net 100.00, tax 20.00, gross 120.00, due date 2026-12-03 and status Unpaid","when":"Staff move it to Delivered on 2026-11-03"},{"given":"A Confirmed order","id":"AC-50.2","level":"api","then":"No invoice exists for that order","when":"The buyer lists invoices"},{"given":"An invoice created at tax rate 20%","id":"AC-50.3","level":"api","then":"That invoice still shows tax 20.00","when":"An administrator changes the tax rate to 21%"}],"ears":"When an order becomes Delivered, the portal shall create one invoice with a unique invoice number, the customer, billing address, order number, invoice date, lines with quantities and net prices, net total, tax at the configured rate, gross total, a due date of the invoice date plus the configured payment-terms days, and status Unpaid.","id":"REQ-50","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","Q-2","Q-4","ASM-18","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An unpaid invoice with due date 2026-12-03","id":"AC-51.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns Unpaid and Overdue","when":"The invoice status calculation is called for 2026-12-03 and 2026-12-04"},{"given":"An invoice paid on 2026-11-20 with due date 2026-12-03","id":"AC-51.2","level":"unit","then":"It returns Paid","when":"The calculation is called for 2027-01-10"}],"ears":"The portal shall report an unpaid invoice as Unpaid up to and including its due date and as Overdue from the day after its due date.","id":"REQ-51","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A with one Paid, one Unpaid and one Overdue invoice from orders of 2 buyers","id":"AC-52.1","level":"api","then":"All 3 invoices are listed with all listed fields and statuses Paid, Unpaid and Overdue","when":"Buyer A1 opens the invoice list"}],"ears":"When a customer buyer opens the invoice list, the portal shall list all invoices of the buyer's company with invoice number, order number, invoice date, due date, gross total and payment status.","id":"REQ-52","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-16","Q-1","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An invoice of company A","id":"AC-53.1","level":"api","then":"The response has content type application/pdf and the extracted text contains all listed fields","when":"A buyer of A downloads it"}],"ears":"When a customer buyer or office staff user downloads an invoice, the portal shall return a PDF containing the invoice number, invoice date, due date, customer, billing address, order number, lines, net total, tax line and gross total.","id":"REQ-53","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Invoices of companies A and B in all three statuses","id":"AC-54.1","level":"api","then":"Only company A's Overdue invoices are returned","when":"Staff filter by company A and Overdue"}],"ears":"When office staff open the invoice list, the portal shall list invoices of all customers, filterable by customer and payment status.","id":"REQ-54","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Overdue invoice","id":"AC-55.1","level":"api","then":"The invoice shows Paid, payment date 2026-12-10 and recorded by S1","when":"Staff user S1 marks it paid with payment date 2026-12-10"},{"given":"An Unpaid invoice","id":"AC-55.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected and the status is unchanged","when":"Staff mark it paid without a payment date, or with a date after today"},{"given":"A Paid invoice","id":"AC-55.3","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected and the recorded payment is unchanged","when":"Staff mark it paid again"}],"ears":"When office staff mark an Unpaid or Overdue invoice as paid with a payment date, the portal shall set the invoice to Paid and record the payment date and the recording user.","id":"REQ-55","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An administrator","id":"AC-56.1","level":"api","then":"A buyer finds it by searching its code","when":"The administrator adds a product with all listed fields and assigns a price"},{"given":"An existing product with code BRK-1023","id":"AC-56.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected as a duplicate code","when":"The administrator adds another product with code BRK-1023"},{"given":"Product R in a past order","id":"AC-56.3","level":"api","then":"R is absent from catalogue and search, adding R to a basket is rejected, and the past order still shows R","when":"The administrator retires R"}],"ears":"Where a user has the administrator role, the portal shall let that user add, edit and retire products with name, internal ID, manufacturer part number, distributor product code, description, category, manufacturer, unit of sale and pack size.","id":"REQ-56","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An administrator","id":"AC-57.1","level":"api","then":"Before retirement buyers can filter by 'Exhaust' and get X; after retirement 'Exhaust' is absent from the category list","when":"The administrator creates 'Exhaust', assigns product X to it, then retires 'Exhaust'"},{"given":"An administrator","id":"AC-57.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected because categories are single-level","when":"The administrator creates a category with a parent category"}],"ears":"Where a user has the administrator role, the portal shall let that user create, edit and retire single-level categories and assign each product to one category.","id":"REQ-57","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17","ASM-10","ASM-33"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P with image img1.png","id":"AC-58.1","level":"api","then":"The catalogue entry for P returns img2 as its image","when":"The administrator uploads a 2 MB img2.jpg for P"},{"given":"Product P","id":"AC-58.2","level":"api","then":"Both uploads are rejected and P's image is unchanged","when":"The administrator uploads a 6 MB PNG, and separately a GIF"}],"ears":"When an administrator uploads a product image that is JPEG, PNG or WebP and at most 5 MB, the portal shall store it as the product's image, replacing any previous image.","id":"REQ-58","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P with no compatibility records","id":"AC-59.1","level":"api","then":"P's detail shows the 2 remaining records and vehicle search finds P only for those 2 vehicles","when":"The administrator adds 3 records and removes 1"}],"ears":"Where a user has the administrator role, the portal shall let that user add and remove vehicle compatibility records of make, model, model year, engine, fuel type and variant on a product, with any number of records per product.","id":"REQ-59","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17","ASM-15","ASM-34"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An administrator","id":"AC-60.1","level":"api","then":"The company is returned with those values","when":"The administrator creates company 'Workshop Alpha' ACC-100 with all listed fields"},{"given":"Company ACC-100 exists","id":"AC-60.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected as a duplicate account number","when":"The administrator creates another company with ACC-100"}],"ears":"Where a user has the administrator role, the portal shall let that user create and edit customer companies with name, account number, primary contact, contact email, contact phone, billing address, assigned price list and active/inactive status.","id":"REQ-60","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A with one address","id":"AC-61.1","level":"api","then":"A buyer of A sees 'Depot 2' among checkout address options","when":"A staff user adds address 'Depot 2' with label, lines, city, region, postal code, country, contact person and phone"},{"given":"Address 'Depot 2' used by a past order","id":"AC-61.2","level":"api","then":"It is absent from checkout options and the past order still shows it","when":"An administrator deactivates it"}],"ears":"Where a user has the office staff or administrator role, the portal shall let that user add, edit and deactivate delivery addresses of a customer company.","id":"REQ-61","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer A1 with 2 orders","id":"AC-62.1","level":"api","then":"A1 is listed as Deactivated and the 2 orders remain visible to colleagues and staff","when":"An administrator deactivates A1"},{"given":"Deactivated user A1","id":"AC-62.2","level":"api","then":"A1 can sign in again","when":"An administrator reactivates A1"},{"given":"Office staff user S1","id":"AC-62.3","level":"api","then":"S1's next call to an administrator function succeeds","when":"An administrator changes S1's role to administrator"}],"ears":"Where a user has the administrator role, the portal shall let that user list users with role, company and account status, change a user's role, link a customer buyer to a customer company, and deactivate and reactivate users.","id":"REQ-62","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Threshold 5 and product P with quantity 8 (In stock)","id":"AC-63.1","level":"api","then":"P is shown as Low stock","when":"The administrator sets the threshold to 10"},{"given":"Cutoff 14:00 and no holidays","id":"AC-63.2","level":"api","then":"The earliest date is Wednesday","when":"The administrator adds Tuesday as a holiday and a buyer checks the earliest date on Monday 13:00"},{"given":"Payment terms 30 days","id":"AC-63.3","level":"api","then":"The new invoice's due date is 2026-11-17","when":"The administrator sets 14 days and an order then becomes Delivered on 2026-11-03"}],"ears":"Where a user has the administrator role, the portal shall let that user set the low-stock threshold, delivery cutoff time, business timezone, holiday dates, tax rate, payment-terms days, reset-link expiry, invitation-link expiry and stock import location.","id":"REQ-63","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-4","ASM-8","ASM-11","ASM-23","ASM-25","Q-2","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P priced 42.00 on 'Standard'","id":"AC-64.1","level":"api","then":"One audit entry exists with AD1, the time, the price entity of P on 'Standard', and 42.00→45.00","when":"Administrator AD1 changes the price to 45.00"},{"given":"Company A active","id":"AC-64.2","level":"api","then":"One audit entry shows the status field active→inactive with the administrator and time","when":"An administrator sets it inactive"}],"ears":"When a product, category, vehicle compatibility record, price list, price, customer company, delivery address or user account is created, changed, retired or deactivated, the portal shall write one audit log entry holding the acting user, timestamp, entity type and id, and each changed field's previous and new value.","id":"REQ-64","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Audit entries for products and customers","id":"AC-65.1","level":"api","then":"Only product entries in that range are returned","when":"An administrator filters by entity type 'product' and a date range"},{"given":"An audit entry","id":"AC-65.2","level":"api","then":"The update/delete is rejected (405 or 404) with the entry unchanged, and the staff call returns 403","when":"An administrator sends an update or delete request for it, and an office staff user lists the audit log"}],"ears":"The portal shall show audit log entries only to administrators, filterable by entity type and date range, with no function to edit or delete an entry.","id":"REQ-65","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"2 Received, 1 Confirmed, 1 Picking, 0 Out for delivery orders, 2 of them due today, 3 Unpaid and 1 Overdue invoice, latest import Failed","id":"AC-66.1","level":"api","then":"It returns 2, 1, 1, 0, 2 due today, 3 Unpaid, 1 Overdue and latest import Failed","when":"Staff open the dashboard"}],"ears":"When office staff open the dashboard, the portal shall show the counts of orders in Received, Confirmed, Picking and Out for delivery status, of orders due for delivery today, of Unpaid and Overdue invoices, and the outcome of the latest stock import.","id":"REQ-66","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"In November: company A with 2 Delivered orders (100.00, 50.00) and 1 Cancelled order; company B with 1 Delivered order (80.00)","id":"AC-67.1","level":"api","then":"Both show A: 2 orders, 150.00 and B: 1 order, 80.00","when":"Staff request the November sales report and its CSV export"}],"ears":"When an office staff user or administrator requests the sales report for a date range, the portal shall list the order count and net sales of Delivered orders per customer, filterable by customer and exportable as CSV.","id":"REQ-67","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-2","ASM-31"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"In November: P sold 3 at 42.00 and 2 at 45.00 in Delivered orders, and 5 in a Cancelled order","id":"AC-68.1","level":"api","then":"Both show P with quantity 5 and net sales 216.00","when":"Staff request the November product report filtered to P's category and its CSV export"}],"ears":"When an office staff user or administrator requests the product report for a date range, the portal shall list the quantity sold and net sales per product from Delivered orders, filterable by category and exportable as CSV.","id":"REQ-68","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-2","ASM-31"]}],"suggestions":["Decide whether a password reset is allowed while an account is locked, and whether it lifts the lock.","Consider letting signed-in users change their own password.","Define a password policy, for example minimum length and complexity.","Add date and status filters to the customer order history (the request recommends these but leaves them open).","Email administrators when a stock import fails, in addition to showing the failure on the dashboard.","Archive or rename processed stock files so the same file is not imported twice.","Agree the exact columns of the delivery-list CSV and the content of each email template with operations.","Decide whether staff can record a payment method when marking an invoice paid.","Revisit saved basket templates in a later release once the private/shared question (ASM-20) is settled."]},{"assumptions":["ASM-13 (basket kept on the server across sessions) wins over the conflicting ASM-29 (basket kept for the browser session only), because the request asks for the basket to persist when the customer navigates away.","ASM-5 and ASM-26 agree: unknown identifiers are skipped and listed, and the import is recorded as 'succeeded with warnings'.","Q-7 and ASM-3 agree: a product with no price is shown, marked 'Price on request', and can't be added to the basket. The same applies to every product when the company's assigned price list is deactivated.","A product with no row in any successful import counts as Out of stock (quantity absent).","Order emails go to the buyer who placed the order. For staff-created orders they go to the customer company's contact email.","Tax is worked out once per invoice on the net subtotal and rounded half-up to 2 decimal places.","Default payment terms are 30 days, default tax rate is 20% and the default image size limit is 5 MB, all configurable. These defaults are illustrative and need confirmation.","Staff can't remove the last line of an order by editing. To withdraw a whole order they reject it, which cancels it with a reason.","When a repeated order's line exceeds current stock, the line is added at the available quantity and flagged. If the product is already in the basket, quantities are added together, still capped at stock.","The 'management' audience for reporting is office staff and administrators. There is no separate management role.","Order notes are free text of up to 500 characters.","Payment method is not recorded in release 1. Only payment date and recording user are kept."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 response time ≤ 1 s for search, category and vehicle queries with 50,000 active products and 50 concurrent users","text":"Catalogue search and filter responses stay quick at the expected catalogue size."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"0 plaintext or reversibly encrypted passwords in storage; Argon2id or bcrypt with cost ≥ 12","text":"Passwords are stored only as salted adaptive hashes."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"100% of requests served over TLS 1.2 or higher; plain HTTP requests redirected with 301","text":"All portal traffic is encrypted in transit."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"Session invalidated after 30 minutes without activity (configurable)","text":"Idle sessions expire."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"Tokens carry ≥ 128 bits of randomness and are stored hashed","text":"Reset and invitation links cannot be guessed."},{"id":"NFR-6","metric":"A 100,000-row CSV is validated and applied within 10 minutes","text":"The nightly stock import finishes within the overnight window."},{"id":"NFR-7","metric":"p95 PDF download time ≤ 5 s for invoices of up to 200 lines","text":"Invoice PDFs are produced on request without long waits."},{"id":"NFR-8","metric":"All amounts stored as fixed-point decimals with 2 decimal places; 0 floating-point money fields","text":"Money amounts are exact."},{"id":"NFR-9","metric":"0 API operations that delete these records","text":"Order, invoice, timeline, amendment and audit records cannot be deleted through the portal."}],"outOfScope":["Customer Account Manager role; every buyer sees all of their own company's orders and invoices instead (Q-1)","Saved basket templates and template sharing; repeat order covers re-ordering (ASM-1, ASM-20)","Customers creating or editing their own delivery addresses (Q-3)","Online card payments and payment method capture","Backorders and ordering above the imported stock quantity (ASM-7)","Stock reservation or reducing stock figures when orders are placed (ASM-22)","Writing stock or any other data back to the ERP","Route planning for deliveries","SMS or push notifications; email only from fixed templates (ASM-14, ASM-21)","Social sign-in and single sign-on (ASM-12)","Nested categories (ASM-10, ASM-33)","Importing vehicle compatibility data from an external source (ASM-15, ASM-34)","Volume pricing, promotional pricing, discounts and price effective dates","Custom report builder (ASM-2, ASM-31)","Migrating existing customers, products, prices or past orders; the system starts empty with seed data (ASM-16)","Reproducing an existing client invoice template; a standard layout carrying the REQ-56 fields is used"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active Customer Buyer with email buyer@a.test and password 'Correct#Pass1'","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"The response is 200 with a session, and GET /me with that session returns the buyer's user id, role and company","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called with those credentials"},{"given":"The same buyer, and no account for nobody@a.test","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"Both responses are 401 with the same message 'Invalid email or password' and no session is created","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called once with a wrong password for buyer@a.test and once with nobody@a.test"}],"ears":"When a user submits an email address and password that match an active account, the portal shall start an authenticated session for that user.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active account with 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"The response is rejected with a message saying the account is temporarily locked, and no session is created","when":"The correct password is submitted 1 minute later"},{"given":"An account locked at 10:00","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 200 with a session and the failed-attempt count is reset to 0","when":"The correct password is submitted at 10:15 or later (test clock advanced)"},{"given":"An account with 4 failed attempts followed by 1 successful sign-in","id":"AC-2.3","level":"api","then":"The account is not locked and a 5th attempt with the correct password succeeds","when":"4 more wrong passwords are submitted"}],"ears":"If 5 consecutive sign-in attempts for an account fail, then the portal shall lock that account for 15 minutes.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active account buyer@a.test","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The response is 202 and the test mailbox receives 1 email to buyer@a.test containing a reset link","when":"POST /auth/password-reset is called with buyer@a.test"},{"given":"No account for nobody@a.test","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 202 with the same body as AC-3.1 and no email is sent","when":"POST /auth/password-reset is called with nobody@a.test"}],"ears":"When a password reset is requested for an email address that belongs to an active account, the portal shall email that address a single-use reset link that expires after the configured reset expiry (default 60 minutes).","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-11","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A reset link issued 10 minutes ago","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The response confirms the change; sign-in with the old password returns 401 and sign-in with the new password returns 200","when":"A new password is submitted through it"},{"given":"A reset link already used once, and another issued 61 minutes ago","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"Both responses are 400 and the account password is unchanged","when":"A new password is submitted through each"}],"ears":"When a user submits a new password through a reset link that is valid, unused and unexpired, the portal shall replace the account's password with the new password.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An administrator session and customer company A","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"The response is 201, the user is listed with status Invited, and the test mailbox receives 1 invitation email to new@a.test","when":"POST /admin/invitations is called for new@a.test with role Customer Buyer and company A"},{"given":"An administrator session","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 400 and no email is sent","when":"An invitation is created with role Customer Buyer and no company, or with role 'Account Manager'"}],"ears":"When an administrator invites a user with name, email, role (Customer Buyer, Office Staff or Administrator) and, for a Customer Buyer, a customer company, the portal shall email that user an invitation link that expires after the configured invitation expiry (default 7 days).","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","Q-1","ASM-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An invitation link issued 2 days ago","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"The user's status becomes Active and sign-in with that password returns 200","when":"The invitee sets a password through it"},{"given":"An invitation link issued 8 days ago","id":"AC-6.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 400 and the user remains Invited","when":"The invitee sets a password through it"}],"ears":"When an invited user sets a password through a valid, unexpired invitation link, the portal shall activate that user's account.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user with status Invited and invitation link L1","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"A new email with link L2 is sent; setting a password via L1 returns 400 and via L2 activates the account","when":"The administrator resends the invitation"}],"ears":"When an administrator resends an invitation, the portal shall invalidate the previous invitation link and email a new one.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","ASM-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in buyer with session S","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"GET /me returns 401","when":"POST /auth/sign-out is called with S and then GET /me is called with S"}],"ears":"When a signed-in user signs out, the portal shall invalidate that user's session.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A buyer with an open session who is then deactivated by an administrator","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"Both requests return 401 and the sign-in message states the account is inactive","when":"The buyer calls GET /basket with the open session and then tries to sign in"},{"given":"Customer company A set to inactive, with buyer U who placed order O","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"U's sign-in is rejected, and the staff call returns order O unchanged","when":"U tries to sign in, and office staff call GET /staff/orders/O"}],"ears":"If a deactivated user, or a user whose customer company is inactive, signs in or makes a request with an existing session, then the portal shall reject the request.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer of company A, and order OB and invoice IB of company B","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"Each response is 404 with no fields of OB or IB in the body","when":"The buyer calls GET /orders/OB, GET /invoices/IB and GET /invoices/IB/pdf"},{"given":"Companies A and B each with orders, invoices and addresses","id":"AC-10.2","level":"api","then":"Every returned item belongs to company A","when":"The buyer of A lists orders, invoices and addresses"}],"ears":"If a Customer Buyer requests an order, invoice, invoice PDF, price, delivery address or company account record belonging to a different customer company, then the portal shall respond with not found and return none of that record's data.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-5","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Customer Buyer session and an Office Staff session","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"Both responses are 403 and no data is changed","when":"The buyer calls GET /staff/orders and the staff user calls POST /admin/price-lists"}],"ears":"If a user calls an office-staff or administrator function without holding the required role, then the portal shall reject the call with 403.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product 'Front Brake Pad Set', code BP-1042, part number 0986494, brand Bosch, and a retired product 'Rear Brake Pad Set'","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"Each search returns 'Front Brake Pad Set', and no search returns the retired product","when":"The buyer searches 'pad', '1042', '0986' and 'BOSCH'"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer searches the catalogue with a text term, the portal shall return the active products whose name, distributor product code, manufacturer part number or manufacturer/brand contains the term, ignoring case.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-2","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active products P1 in Filters and P2 in Brake system","id":"AC-13.1","level":"api","then":"The results are [P1], then [P2], then both P1 and P2","when":"The buyer filters by Filters, then by Brake system, then clears the filter"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer filters the catalogue by a category, the portal shall return only active products assigned to that category.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"P1 compatible with Ford Focus 2018 1.0 EcoBoost petrol, P2 compatible with Ford Focus 2018 1.5 TDCi diesel, P3 with no compatibility","id":"AC-14.1","level":"api","then":"The first search returns P1 and P2 only; the second returns P2 only","when":"The buyer searches Ford/Focus/2018, then Ford/Focus/2018 with fuel type diesel"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer searches by vehicle make, model and year, optionally narrowed by engine, fuel type or variant, the portal shall return only active products marked compatible with a matching vehicle.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P1 priced 12.50 on company A's price list with stock status Low stock","id":"AC-15.1","level":"api","then":"P1's entry contains image URL, name, code, manufacturer, unit, pack size, price 12.50 and status 'Low stock'","when":"A buyer of company A lists the catalogue"}],"ears":"The portal shall return, for each product in catalogue results, its image URL, name, distributor product code, manufacturer, unit of sale, pack size, the requesting company's price and its stock status.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product P1 with imported quantity 0 and 2 compatible vehicles","id":"AC-16.1","level":"api","then":"The response is 200 with all listed fields, stock status 'Out of stock' and both vehicles","when":"A buyer calls GET /products/P1"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer opens an active product, the portal shall return its image, name, code, manufacturer, description, unit, pack size, the company's price, stock status and compatible vehicles, including when the product is Out of stock.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A on list Standard (P1 = 20.00) and company B on list Fleet (P1 = 17.00)","id":"AC-17.1","level":"api","then":"Buyer A sees 20.00 and buyer B sees 17.00, both marked as net prices","when":"A buyer of A and a buyer of B each open P1"}],"ears":"The portal shall price each product for a Customer Buyer at the net price on the active price list assigned to the buyer's company.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P2 not on company A's price list","id":"AC-18.1","level":"api","then":"P2 is shown with no price and the 'Price on request' marker, and the add returns 422 with the basket unchanged","when":"A buyer of A opens P2 and calls POST /basket/lines for P2"},{"given":"Company A's assigned price list is deactivated","id":"AC-18.2","level":"api","then":"Every product is marked 'Price on request'","when":"A buyer of A lists the catalogue"}],"ears":"If a product has no price on an active price list assigned to the buyer's company, then the portal shall mark the product as 'Price on request' and reject adding it to the basket.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11","Q-7","ASM-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Price list Fleet with P1 = 17.00 assigned to company B","id":"AC-19.1","level":"api","then":"A buyer of B opening P1 sees 16.50","when":"The administrator edits P1 to 16.50"},{"given":"Price list Fleet already containing P1","id":"AC-19.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 409 and P1 keeps a single price","when":"The administrator adds P1 to Fleet again"}],"ears":"When an administrator creates, renames or deactivates a price list, or adds, edits or removes a product price on it, the portal shall store the change while allowing at most one price per product per price list.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A on Standard (P1 = 20.00) with P1 in a buyer's basket, and Dealer list with P1 = 18.00","id":"AC-20.1","level":"api","then":"The P1 line shows 18.00","when":"The administrator assigns Dealer to A and the buyer then views the basket"}],"ears":"When an administrator assigns a different price list to a customer company, the portal shall price that company's later catalogue, basket and checkout requests from the newly assigned list.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A low-stock threshold of 5","id":"AC-21.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns Out of stock, Out of stock, Low stock, Low stock and In stock","when":"The stock status classifier's public classify method is called with quantities 0, null, 1, 5 and 6"}],"ears":"The portal shall classify a product as Out of stock when its latest imported quantity is 0 or absent, as Low stock when it is from 1 up to and including the configured low-stock threshold, and as In stock when it is above the threshold.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-12","ASM-4","ASM-24"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"P1 stored with quantity 10 and a valid file in the pickup location listing P1 = 3 (threshold 5)","id":"AC-22.1","level":"job","then":"P1 has quantity 3 and status Low stock, and an import record with outcome 'succeeded' and the run time exists","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"When the scheduled stock import finds a valid ERP CSV file in the configured folder or SFTP location, the portal shall replace the stored stock quantities with the file's quantities, update each product's stock status and record the import as succeeded.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","ASM-6","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"P1 stored with quantity 10 and a file whose second row has quantity 'abc'","id":"AC-23.1","level":"job","then":"P1 still has quantity 10, no product quantity changed, and an import record with outcome 'failed' and a reason naming row 2 exists","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"If the ERP stock file is unreadable, lacks a required column, or contains a non-integer or negative quantity, then the portal shall keep all previously imported stock data unchanged and record the import as failed with the reason.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A file listing P1 = 4 and unknown identifier ZZ-999 = 7","id":"AC-24.1","level":"job","then":"P1 has quantity 4, and the import record has outcome 'succeeded with warnings' listing ZZ-999","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"If an otherwise valid ERP stock file contains product identifiers the portal does not recognise, then the portal shall apply the recognised rows, skip the unrecognised ones and record the import as succeeded with warnings listing the skipped identifiers.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","ASM-5","ASM-26"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"One succeeded, one failed and one succeeded-with-warnings import","id":"AC-25.1","level":"api","then":"All 3 runs are returned newest first with outcome and reason or skipped identifiers","when":"Office staff call GET /staff/stock-imports"}],"ears":"When office staff or an administrator list stock imports, the portal shall return each import run with its time, outcome and failure reason or skipped identifiers.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A buyer who added P1 x 2 to the basket","id":"AC-26.1","level":"api","then":"GET /basket returns P1 x 2","when":"The buyer signs out and signs in again from a new session"}],"ears":"The portal shall store each Customer Buyer's basket on the server so that it is kept across sign-outs and sessions.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"P1 at 10.00 and P2 at 5.50 with enough stock","id":"AC-27.1","level":"api","then":"After the adds the subtotal is 36.50 with line totals 20.00 and 16.50 and a note that tax is added on the invoice; after the removal the subtotal is 16.50","when":"The buyer adds P1 x 2 and P2 x 3, then removes P1"},{"given":"P1 in the basket","id":"AC-27.2","level":"api","then":"Each request returns 400 and the basket is unchanged","when":"The buyer sets its quantity to 0, -1 or 1.5"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer adds a product, changes a line quantity or removes a line, the portal shall return the updated basket with each line's unit net price, line total and the net subtotal.","id":"REQ-27","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-4","I-13","ASM-30"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"P1 with imported quantity 4 and P3 with quantity 0","id":"AC-28.1","level":"api","then":"Both requests return 422 stating the available quantity, and the basket is unchanged","when":"The buyer adds P1 x 5 and P3 x 1"}],"ears":"If a Customer Buyer adds or sets a quantity greater than the product's latest imported stock quantity, or adds an Out of stock product, then the portal shall reject the change and leave the basket unchanged.","id":"REQ-28","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-13","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Cut-off 14:00, weekends non-working, no holidays","id":"AC-29.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns Tuesday, Wednesday, the following Tuesday and the following Monday","when":"The delivery-date calculator's public earliest-date method is called for Monday 13:59, Monday 14:00, Friday 15:00 and Saturday 10:00"},{"given":"Cut-off 14:00 and Tuesday entered as a holiday","id":"AC-29.2","level":"unit","then":"It returns Wednesday","when":"The method is called for Monday 13:00"},{"given":"Business timezone Europe/London during summer time","id":"AC-29.3","level":"unit","then":"It returns Tuesday and Wednesday","when":"The method is called for Monday 12:30 UTC (13:30 local) and Monday 13:30 UTC (14:30 local)"}],"ears":"The portal shall set the earliest delivery date to the next working day for orders placed before the configured cut-off time (default 14:00) in the configured business timezone, and to the second working day after the order time for orders placed at or after the cut-off.","id":"REQ-29","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-8","ASM-23"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A valid basket on Monday 15:00 with earliest date Wednesday","id":"AC-30.1","level":"api","then":"Both submissions return 422, no order is created, and the response lists the earliest date","when":"The buyer submits checkout with Tuesday, then with Saturday"}],"ears":"If the delivery date chosen at checkout is earlier than the earliest delivery date or falls on a non-working day, then the portal shall reject the submission.","id":"REQ-30","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-23"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A with active address AD1 and deactivated address AD2, and company B with address BD1","id":"AC-31.1","level":"api","then":"The first two return 422 with no order created; the third creates the order with AD1","when":"A buyer of A submits checkout with AD2, then BD1, then AD1"},{"given":"A Customer Buyer session","id":"AC-31.2","level":"api","then":"Both return 403 and the addresses are unchanged","when":"The buyer calls POST /addresses or PUT /addresses/AD1"}],"ears":"If a checkout submission names a delivery address that is not an active delivery address of the buyer's company, then the portal shall reject the submission.","id":"REQ-31","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A buyer who reviewed P1 at 10.00, after which the administrator changed P1 to 11.00","id":"AC-32.1","level":"api","then":"The response is 409 with P1 at 11.00 and the new subtotal, and no order is created","when":"The buyer submits checkout"},{"given":"The situation of AC-32.1 after the buyer reviews the updated prices","id":"AC-32.2","level":"api","then":"An order is created with P1 at 11.00","when":"The buyer submits checkout again"}],"ears":"If any basket line's current price differs from the price the buyer last reviewed when the order is submitted, then the portal shall reject the submission and return the updated prices for the buyer to review before resubmitting.","id":"REQ-32","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-13","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket with P1 x 4, after a stock import reduced P1 to quantity 2","id":"AC-33.1","level":"api","then":"The response is 422 naming the P1 line with available quantity 2, and no order is created","when":"The buyer submits checkout"}],"ears":"If, at checkout submission, a line quantity exceeds the latest imported stock quantity or a line's product is retired, Out of stock or without a price, then the portal shall reject the submission and identify each affected line.","id":"REQ-33","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-13","ASM-7","ASM-22"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A valid basket with P1 x 2 at 10.00, address AD1, delivery date Wednesday and note 'Rear door'","id":"AC-34.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains an order number not used by any other order; GET /orders/{id} shows status Received, P1 x 2 at 10.00, AD1, Wednesday and the note; the basket is empty","when":"The buyer submits checkout"},{"given":"The order created in AC-34.1","id":"AC-34.2","level":"api","then":"The order appears in the list","when":"Office staff call GET /staff/orders?status=Received"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer submits a checkout that passes all validation, the portal shall create an order in status Received with a unique order number, its lines at order-time net prices, the delivery address, the delivery date and the optional note.","id":"REQ-34","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-4","I-13","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order O with P1 at 10.00","id":"AC-35.1","level":"api","then":"GET /orders/O still shows P1 at 10.00 and the original total","when":"The administrator changes P1 to 12.00 on the company's list"}],"ears":"When a price on a price list changes, the portal shall keep the stored prices of existing orders and invoices unchanged.","id":"REQ-35","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Orders in Received, Delivered and Cancelled status","id":"AC-36.1","level":"api","then":"Each request returns 409 and each status is unchanged","when":"Office staff request Received→Picking, Delivered→Picking and Cancelled→Confirmed"},{"given":"An order in Confirmed status","id":"AC-36.2","level":"api","then":"The order status becomes Picking","when":"Office staff request Picking"}],"ears":"If a status change is requested that is neither one step forward along Received, Confirmed, Picking, Out for delivery, Delivered nor a permitted cancellation, then the portal shall reject the change and leave the order status unchanged.","id":"REQ-36","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-27"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order placed by buyer U and confirmed by staff user S","id":"AC-37.1","level":"api","then":"The timeline holds 2 entries in order: Received by U and Confirmed by S, each with a timestamp","when":"GET /orders/{id} is called"}],"ears":"When an order changes status, the portal shall append a timeline entry recording the new status, the date and time, and the user or system that made the change.","id":"REQ-37","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-8","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Orders for companies A and B in statuses Received and Picking on different dates","id":"AC-38.1","level":"api","then":"Only A's Received orders are returned, each with the listed fields","when":"Office staff call GET /staff/orders filtered by customer A and status Received"}],"ears":"When office staff list orders, the portal shall return the orders of all customer companies with order number, customer, order date, requested delivery date, net total and status, filterable by customer, order date range and status.","id":"REQ-38","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order with P1 x 4","id":"AC-39.1","level":"api","then":"The order shows P1 x 2 with the recalculated total, and its amendments list holds an entry with the staff user, time, field 'quantity P1', before 4 and after 2","when":"Office staff change P1 to 2"},{"given":"A Confirmed order","id":"AC-39.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 409 and the order is unchanged","when":"Office staff try to change a line quantity"},{"given":"A Received order","id":"AC-39.3","level":"api","then":"The response is 422 and the order is unchanged","when":"Office staff set a delivery date before the earliest delivery date or an address of another company"}],"ears":"While an order is in Received status, the portal shall allow office staff to change line quantities, remove lines, change the delivery date and delivery address and edit the note, recording each amendment with the user, time and before and after values.","id":"REQ-39","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","I-8","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order with P1 x 2 and P1 stock 5","id":"AC-40.1","level":"api","then":"The status is Confirmed with the staff user and timestamp recorded, and a buyer cancellation attempt then returns 409","when":"Office staff confirm it"},{"given":"A Received order with P1 x 6 and P1 stock 5","id":"AC-40.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 422 naming the P1 line and the status stays Received","when":"Office staff confirm it"}],"ears":"When office staff confirm a Received order whose line quantities are within the latest imported stock and whose customer company is active, the portal shall set the order to Confirmed and record who confirmed it and when.","id":"REQ-40","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order placed by buyer U whose P1 quantity staff changed from 4 to 2","id":"AC-41.1","level":"api","then":"The test mailbox receives 1 email to U containing the order number, the lines, the delivery date and address, and the text showing P1 changed from 4 to 2","when":"Office staff confirm it"}],"ears":"When an order becomes Confirmed, the portal shall email the order's buyer a confirmation containing the order number, lines, quantities, delivery date, delivery address and any quantity changes made by staff.","id":"REQ-41","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-14","ASM-14","ASM-21"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Confirmed order","id":"AC-42.1","level":"api","then":"The status is Cancelled and the order shows the reason, the staff user and the time","when":"Office staff reject it with reason 'Part discontinued'"},{"given":"A Received order and a Picking order","id":"AC-42.2","level":"api","then":"The first returns 400 and the second returns 409; both statuses are unchanged","when":"Office staff reject the Received order with an empty reason, and the Picking order with a reason"}],"ears":"When office staff reject an order in Received or Confirmed status with a reason, the portal shall set the order to Cancelled and record the reason, the user and the time.","id":"REQ-42","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","I-14","ASM-9","ASM-27","ASM-28"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order placed by buyer U","id":"AC-43.1","level":"api","then":"The test mailbox receives 1 email to U containing the order number and 'Account on hold'","when":"Office staff reject it with reason 'Account on hold'"}],"ears":"When office staff reject an order, the portal shall email the order's buyer a cancellation notice containing the order number and the reason.","id":"REQ-43","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-14","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Picking order placed by buyer U","id":"AC-44.1","level":"api","then":"The test mailbox receives 1 email to U containing the order number and the words 'out for delivery'","when":"Office staff set it to Out for delivery"}],"ears":"When an order changes to Out for delivery, the portal shall email the order's buyer a notice identifying the order and stating that it is out for delivery.","id":"REQ-44","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-14","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A on a list with P1 = 9.00, address AD1 and P1 stock 10","id":"AC-45.1","level":"api","then":"An order in Received status is created with P1 at 9.00 and created-by set to the staff user, and a buyer of A sees it in GET /orders","when":"Office staff submit an order for A with P1 x 3, AD1 and a valid delivery date"},{"given":"Company A and P1 stock 10","id":"AC-45.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 422 and no order is created","when":"Office staff submit an order for A with P1 x 11"}],"ears":"When office staff submit an order on behalf of a customer company, the portal shall create it with the same pricing, stock, delivery-date and address validation as a buyer checkout and record it as created by that staff user.","id":"REQ-45","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","I-14","I-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"P1 at 17.00 on company B's list with stock 3 (threshold 5)","id":"AC-46.1","level":"api","then":"The response shows price 17.00, quantity 3 and status Low stock","when":"Office staff call GET /staff/products/P1?customer=B"}],"ears":"When office staff look up a product for a chosen customer company, the portal shall return that company's price for the product and the product's latest imported stock quantity and stock status.","id":"REQ-46","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Companies 'Smith Motors' (ACC-1001) and 'Fleetway Ltd' (ACC-2002)","id":"AC-47.1","level":"api","then":"The results are Smith Motors, then Fleetway Ltd","when":"Office staff search 'smith', then '2002'"}],"ears":"When office staff search customer companies by name or account number, the portal shall return the companies whose name or account number contains the term, ignoring case.","id":"REQ-47","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A with orders placed by buyers U1 and U2, one Received and one Delivered","id":"AC-48.1","level":"api","then":"Only the Delivered order is returned, even though U2 placed it, with the listed fields","when":"U1 lists orders filtered by status Delivered"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer lists orders, the portal shall return every order of the buyer's company with order number, order date, delivery date, delivery address, net total and status, filterable by order date range and status.","id":"REQ-48","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Confirmed order of company A with one staff quantity amendment","id":"AC-49.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains every listed field, including the timeline with 2 entries and the amendment with before and after values","when":"A buyer of A calls GET /orders/{id}"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer opens an order of their company, the portal shall return its order number, order date, customer, delivery address, requested delivery date, current status, status timeline, lines with quantities, unit prices and line totals, order total, note and staff amendments.","id":"REQ-49","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order placed by buyer U1 of company A","id":"AC-50.1","level":"api","then":"The status is Cancelled with a timeline entry naming U2","when":"Buyer U2 of company A cancels it"},{"given":"A Confirmed order of company A","id":"AC-50.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 409 with a message to contact the distributor office, and the status stays Confirmed","when":"A buyer of A tries to cancel it"}],"ears":"While an order is in Received status, the portal shall allow any active Customer Buyer of the order's company to cancel it.","id":"REQ-50","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Past order O (placed by colleague U1) with P1 x 2 at 10.00 and retired P4 x 1, where P1 is now 11.00 with stock 10","id":"AC-51.1","level":"api","then":"The basket contains P1 x 2 at 11.00, the response flags P4 as no longer available, and the company's order count is unchanged","when":"Buyer U2 of the same company repeats O"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer repeats an order of their company, the portal shall add that order's still-orderable lines to the buyer's basket at current prices and flag the lines that are retired, Out of stock or without a price, without creating an order.","id":"REQ-51","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15","Q-6","ASM-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Tax rate 20%, payment terms 30 days, and an Out for delivery order with net total 36.50","id":"AC-52.1","level":"api","then":"1 invoice exists with net 36.50, tax 7.30, total 43.80, invoice date 2026-11-02, due date 2026-12-02 and status Unpaid","when":"Office staff set it to Delivered on 2026-11-02"},{"given":"An order in Picking status","id":"AC-52.2","level":"api","then":"No invoice for that order is returned","when":"A buyer of its company lists invoices"}],"ears":"When an order becomes Delivered, the portal shall create exactly one invoice for it containing invoice number, customer, billing address, order number, invoice date, lines with quantities and order-time net prices, net subtotal, a tax line at the configured tax rate, gross total, due date and payment status Unpaid.","id":"REQ-52","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-16","Q-2","Q-4","ASM-18","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Unpaid invoice with due date 2026-12-02","id":"AC-53.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns Unpaid, Overdue and Paid","when":"The invoice status method is evaluated with current dates 2026-12-02 and 2026-12-03, and with 2026-12-03 after it is marked paid"}],"ears":"While an invoice is Unpaid and the current date in the business timezone is after its due date, the portal shall report its payment status as Overdue.","id":"REQ-53","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Overdue invoice","id":"AC-54.1","level":"api","then":"The invoice shows status Paid, payment date 2026-12-05 and the staff user","when":"Office staff mark it paid with payment date 2026-12-05"},{"given":"An Unpaid invoice","id":"AC-54.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 400 and the status stays Unpaid","when":"Office staff mark it paid without a payment date"}],"ears":"When office staff mark an Unpaid or Overdue invoice as paid with a payment date, the portal shall set its status to Paid and record the payment date and the user who recorded it.","id":"REQ-54","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","I-16"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A with one Paid and one Overdue invoice for orders placed by different buyers","id":"AC-55.1","level":"api","then":"Both invoices are returned with the listed fields and statuses Paid and Overdue","when":"A buyer of A calls GET /invoices"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer lists invoices, the portal shall return every invoice of the buyer's company with invoice number, order number, invoice date, due date, total and payment status.","id":"REQ-55","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-16","Q-1","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The invoice from AC-52.1","id":"AC-56.1","level":"api","then":"The response is 200 with content type application/pdf, and the extracted text contains the invoice number, order number, 36.50, 7.30, 43.80 and the due date","when":"A buyer of its company calls GET /invoices/{id}/pdf"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer of the invoice's company or an office staff user downloads an invoice, the portal shall return a PDF containing the invoice number, customer, billing address, order number, invoice date, due date, lines, net subtotal, tax line, total and payment status.","id":"REQ-56","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-16","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Invoices for companies A and B with statuses Paid and Unpaid","id":"AC-57.1","level":"api","then":"Only Unpaid invoices from both companies are returned","when":"Office staff call GET /staff/invoices filtered by status Unpaid"}],"ears":"When office staff list invoices, the portal shall return the invoices of all customer companies, filterable by customer and payment status.","id":"REQ-57","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-16"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An administrator session","id":"AC-58.1","level":"api","then":"GET /products/{id} returns the new description and the other fields as entered","when":"The administrator adds a product with all listed fields and then changes its description"},{"given":"An existing product with code BP-1042","id":"AC-58.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 409","when":"The administrator adds another product with code BP-1042"}],"ears":"When an administrator adds or edits a product, the portal shall store its name, internal product ID, manufacturer part number, unique distributor product code, description, category, manufacturer/brand, unit of sale, pack size and status.","id":"REQ-58","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P1 on Delivered order O and its invoice","id":"AC-59.1","level":"api","then":"P1 is absent from catalogue list and search results, adding P1 to a basket returns 422, and order O and its invoice still show the P1 line","when":"The administrator retires P1"}],"ears":"When an administrator retires a product, the portal shall exclude it from catalogue browsing and search while keeping it on existing orders and invoices.","id":"REQ-59","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An administrator session","id":"AC-60.1","level":"api","then":"After assignment, filtering by Exhaust returns P5; after retirement, Exhaust no longer appears in the category list","when":"The administrator creates category 'Exhaust', assigns P5 to it, then retires 'Exhaust'"},{"given":"An administrator session","id":"AC-60.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 400","when":"The administrator creates a category with a parent category"}],"ears":"When an administrator creates, edits or retires a single-level category or assigns a product to it, the portal shall apply the change to catalogue category filters.","id":"REQ-60","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17","ASM-10","ASM-33"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P1 with image A","id":"AC-61.1","level":"api","then":"Both uploads return 400 and P1 still returns image A","when":"The administrator uploads a 6 MB JPEG and then a 100 KB GIF"},{"given":"Product P1 with image A","id":"AC-61.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 200 and P1's catalogue entry returns the new image URL","when":"The administrator uploads a 1 MB PNG"}],"ears":"If an administrator uploads a product image that is not JPEG, PNG or WebP or is larger than the configured image size limit (default 5 MB), then the portal shall reject the upload and keep the existing image.","id":"REQ-61","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P1 with no compatible vehicles","id":"AC-62.1","level":"api","then":"A vehicle search for VW Golf 2019 returns P1 and a search for Audi A3 2019 does not","when":"The administrator adds VW Golf 2019 and Audi A3 2019, then removes Audi A3 2019"}],"ears":"When an administrator adds or removes a compatible vehicle (make, model, model year, and optionally engine, fuel type and variant) on a product, the portal shall include or exclude that product in vehicle searches matching that vehicle.","id":"REQ-62","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","I-17","ASM-15","ASM-34"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An administrator session","id":"AC-63.1","level":"api","then":"GET /admin/customers/{id} returns all fields as entered","when":"The administrator creates company 'Smith Motors' with account number ACC-1001 and all listed fields"},{"given":"Existing company with account number ACC-1001","id":"AC-63.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 409","when":"The administrator creates another company with ACC-1001"}],"ears":"When an administrator creates or edits a customer company, the portal shall store its name, unique account number, primary contact, contact email, contact phone, billing address, assigned price list and active status.","id":"REQ-63","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A with address AD1","id":"AC-64.1","level":"api","then":"A buyer of A listing checkout addresses gets only AD2","when":"Office staff add AD2 with label, address lines, city, region, postal code, country, contact person and phone, then deactivate AD1"}],"ears":"When office staff or an administrator add, edit or deactivate a delivery address of a customer company, the portal shall offer only that company's active addresses at checkout.","id":"REQ-64","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer U with 3 past orders","id":"AC-65.1","level":"api","then":"While deactivated U cannot sign in; after reactivation U can sign in; staff see all 3 orders throughout","when":"The administrator deactivates U and then reactivates U"},{"given":"User U with role Office Staff and an open session","id":"AC-65.2","level":"api","then":"U's next call to GET /staff/orders returns 403","when":"The administrator changes U's role to Customer Buyer of company A"}],"ears":"When an administrator deactivates, reactivates, changes the role of, or changes the customer company of a user, the portal shall apply the change from that user's next request while keeping all of the user's historical orders and invoices.","id":"REQ-65","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"One invited, one active, one locked and one deactivated user","id":"AC-66.1","level":"api","then":"All 4 are returned with their listed fields and statuses Invited, Active, Locked and Deactivated","when":"The administrator calls GET /admin/users"}],"ears":"When an administrator lists users, the portal shall return each user's name, email, role, customer company and account status (Invited, Active, Locked or Deactivated).","id":"REQ-66","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Cut-off 14:00 and an existing invoice taxed at 20%","id":"AC-67.1","level":"api","then":"An earliest-date request for Monday 13:00 returns Wednesday, a newly created invoice uses 10%, and the existing invoice still shows 20%","when":"The administrator sets cut-off to 12:00 and tax rate to 10%"},{"given":"An Office Staff session","id":"AC-67.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 403","when":"The staff user tries to update the tax rate"}],"ears":"When an administrator updates a system setting (low-stock threshold, delivery cut-off time, business timezone, non-working dates, tax rate, payment terms days, reset and invitation link expiry, image size limit), the portal shall apply the new value only to calculations made after the change.","id":"REQ-67","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-4","ASM-8","ASM-11","ASM-23","Q-2","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P1 with description 'Old'","id":"AC-68.1","level":"api","then":"1 audit entry exists with user X, a timestamp, entity Product/P1, field description, before 'Old' and after 'New'","when":"Administrator X changes the description to 'New'"},{"given":"Company A with price list Standard","id":"AC-68.2","level":"api","then":"1 audit entry exists for Customer/A with field price list, before Standard and after Dealer","when":"The administrator assigns price list Dealer to A"}],"ears":"When a product, category, price list, price, customer company, delivery address or user account is created, changed, retired or deactivated, the portal shall write one audit log entry recording the acting user, time, entity type and id, and each changed field's before and after values.","id":"REQ-68","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Audit entries for products and customers by two administrators","id":"AC-69.1","level":"api","then":"Only product entries are returned, newest first; the same call by office staff returns 403","when":"An administrator calls GET /admin/audit filtered by entity type Product"}],"ears":"When an administrator views the audit log, the portal shall return entries newest first, filterable by entity type, entity id, user and date range.","id":"REQ-69","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","I-17","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"For 2026-11-04: a Confirmed order, a Picking order and a Cancelled order; and a Confirmed order for 2026-11-05","id":"AC-70.1","level":"api","then":"The CSV has a header row with the listed columns and exactly 2 data rows, for the Confirmed and Picking orders","when":"Office staff call GET /staff/delivery-list.csv?date=2026-11-04"}],"ears":"When office staff export the delivery list for a date, the portal shall return a CSV with one row per non-cancelled order due for delivery that date, containing order number, customer, delivery address, contact person, contact phone, delivery date, line summary, note and status.","id":"REQ-70","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"2 Received, 1 Picking, 1 Out for delivery order, 1 order due today, 3 Unpaid and 1 Overdue invoice, and a failed latest import","id":"AC-71.1","level":"api","then":"The response shows 2, 1, 1, 1, 3, 1 and latest import 'failed'","when":"Office staff call GET /staff/dashboard"}],"ears":"When office staff open the dashboard, the portal shall return the counts of Received, Picking and Out for delivery orders, orders due for delivery today, Unpaid and Overdue invoices, and the outcome of the latest stock import.","id":"REQ-71","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"In November: company A orders P1 x 2 at 10.00 and P2 x 1 at 5.00, company B orders P1 x 1 at 9.00, and a cancelled order of B for P2 x 5","id":"AC-72.1","level":"api","then":"Per customer: A 1 order 25.00, B 1 order 9.00; per product: P1 qty 3 value 29.00, P2 qty 1 value 5.00; the CSV holds the same figures","when":"An administrator requests the November sales report and its CSV export"}],"ears":"When office staff or an administrator request the sales report for a date range, the portal shall return, per customer and per product, the number of orders, quantities and net value of non-cancelled orders placed in that range, viewable on screen and exportable as CSV.","id":"REQ-72","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-2","ASM-31"]}],"suggestions":["Confirm how a password-reset request is handled while an account is locked. Assumptions ASM-12 and ASM-32 don't answer this, so the spec doesn't define it.","Rate-limit password-reset and invitation emails per address (e.g. 5 per hour) to stop email flooding.","Consider adding the Customer Account Manager role in a later release, with per-buyer visibility limits.","Consider saved basket templates in a later release (left out by ASM-1).","Consider per-product or per-category low-stock thresholds if one global threshold proves too coarse.","Consider a confirmation step and a reason field for customer cancellations; the confirmation flow is an open point.","Consider letting customers request address changes from inside the portal, routed to staff.","Consider alerting admins by email when a stock import fails or no file arrives by a set time.","Consider extra report filters (e.g. by category or brand) once management's needs are known."]},{"assumptions":["ASM-35: ASM-13 (basket saved per user on the server across sessions) and ASM-29 (basket kept for the browser session only) contradict each other. This spec follows ASM-13 because the request asks for the basket to persist when the customer navigates away. To be confirmed by the product owner.","ASM-36: Order emails (amendment, confirmation, rejection, out for delivery) go to the buyer who placed the order. For staff-created orders they go to the company's contact email.","ASM-37: Delivery list CSV columns are order number, customer, delivery address, contact name, contact phone, delivery date, line summary, note and status. It lists orders in Confirmed, Picking or Out for delivery for the chosen date.","ASM-38: Product images must be JPEG, PNG or WebP and at most 5 MB. There is one image per product, and a new upload replaces the old one.","ASM-39: There is no separate management role. Office staff and administrators can see the sales reports and the staff dashboard.","ASM-40: A stock file is invalid if it is empty, has no identifier or quantity column, or has any non-numeric or negative quantity. An invalid file is rejected as a whole.","ASM-41: Staff can change the delivery date and address only while an order is Received, under the same earliest-date, working-day and own-company-address rules as checkout.","ASM-43: Dashboard figures are orders placed today, orders in Received (awaiting confirmation), Picking, Out for delivery, orders due for delivery today, invoices Unpaid or Overdue, and stock imports that failed in the last 7 days.","Duplicate assumptions were merged: ASM-8 with ASM-23, ASM-4 with ASM-24, ASM-5 with ASM-26, ASM-6 with ASM-25, ASM-10 with ASM-33, ASM-15 with ASM-34, ASM-14 with ASM-21, ASM-2 with ASM-31, ASM-12 with ASM-32, and ASM-18 with ASM-19. ASM-20 (templates private) does not apply because ASM-1 puts templates out of scope.","Money is shown with 2 decimal places, and tax is rounded half-up to 2 decimals on the invoice net subtotal."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 response time ≤ 1.0 s at 20 concurrent users","text":"Catalogue search, category filter and vehicle search respond within a set time on a catalogue of 50,000 active products."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"A 100,000-row CSV is validated and applied in ≤ 10 minutes","text":"Stock import finishes within a set time for a full ERP file."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"0 plaintext or reversibly encrypted passwords in storage; bcrypt cost ≥ 12 or Argon2id with ≥ 64 MB memory","text":"Passwords are stored only as salted adaptive hashes."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"≥ 128 bits of randomness per token; only a hash of the token is stored","text":"Reset and invitation tokens cannot be guessed."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"100% of endpoints served over TLS 1.2 or higher; HTTP requests redirected to HTTPS","text":"All traffic carrying personal or pricing data is encrypted."},{"id":"NFR-6","metric":"Session invalidated after 30 minutes of inactivity","text":"Idle sessions expire."},{"id":"NFR-7","metric":"p95 ≤ 3 s for an invoice of up to 200 lines","text":"Invoice PDF generation time."},{"id":"NFR-8","metric":"≥ 99.5% monthly uptime, 07:00–19:00 business timezone, Monday–Friday","text":"Portal availability during business hours."},{"id":"NFR-9","metric":"0 hard deletes of orders, invoices, timeline entries or audit entries; kept for ≥ 7 years","text":"Order, invoice, timeline and audit records are kept."}],"outOfScope":["Customer Account Manager role (Q-1)","Saved basket templates, request section 16 (ASM-1)","Customers creating or editing their own delivery addresses (Q-3)","Separate 'Rejected' order status (ASM-9, ASM-28)","Nested categories (ASM-10, ASM-33)","Social login or single sign-on (ASM-12, ASM-32)","SMS or push notifications; editable email templates (ASM-14, ASM-21)","Importing vehicle compatibility data from an external source (ASM-15, ASM-34)","Migrating existing customers, products, prices or past orders; the system starts empty with seed data (ASM-16)","Stock reservation or reducing portal stock when orders are placed (ASM-22)","Custom report builder (ASM-2, ASM-31)","Backorders (request section 8: out of scope unless separately agreed)","Online card payments (request section 32)","Delivery route planning (request section 22)","Writing stock or any other data back to the ERP (request section 9)","Volume pricing, promotional pricing, discounts and price effective dates (request section 10, one price per product per price list)","Payment method recording on invoices (request section 32 open point, not asked for)"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active buyer of an active company with email buyer@a.test and password 'Correct#1'","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"The response is a success with a session token or cookie, and a follow-up GET /me returns the buyer's identity and role","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called with those credentials"},{"given":"An active buyer with 3 consecutive failed sign-in attempts","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"The account is not locked after those 4 wrong attempts, because the counter was reset to 0 by the successful sign-in","when":"The buyer signs in with the correct password and then submits 4 wrong passwords"}],"ears":"When a user submits an email address and password that match an active user whose customer company (if any) is active, the portal shall start an authenticated session for that user and reset the user's consecutive failed sign-in counter to 0.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-12","ASM-32"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"No user exists with email nobody@a.test, and buyer@a.test exists","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"Both responses are 401 with the same message body 'Invalid email or password' and neither starts a session","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called once with nobody@a.test and once with buyer@a.test and a wrong password"}],"ears":"If a sign-in attempt uses an unknown email address or a wrong password, then the portal shall reject the attempt with the same generic 'Invalid email or password' message in both cases and add one to the failed-attempt counter of the matching account, if there is one.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active buyer account with 0 failed attempts","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The sixth response is rejected with a 'temporarily locked' message and no session is started","when":"5 sign-ins with a wrong password are submitted, then a sign-in with the correct password is submitted 1 minute later"},{"given":"An account locked at 10:00:00 (test clock)","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"The 10:14:59 attempt is rejected as locked and the 10:15:01 attempt starts a session","when":"The correct password is submitted at 10:14:59 and again at 10:15:01"}],"ears":"If an account reaches 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, then the portal shall lock the account for 15 minutes, rejecting every sign-in attempt during that time, including ones with the correct password, with a message saying the account is temporarily locked.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A buyer whose user record has been deactivated by an admin","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The response is a rejection stating the account is inactive and no session is created","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called with the buyer's correct credentials"},{"given":"An active buyer whose company has been set to inactive","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"The response is a rejection and no session is created","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called with correct credentials"},{"given":"A buyer with a session open who is then deactivated by an admin","id":"AC-4.3","level":"api","then":"The response is 401 or 403 and no order is created","when":"The buyer calls POST /checkout with that session"}],"ears":"If a deactivated user, or a user whose customer company is inactive, submits correct sign-in credentials, then the portal shall refuse sign-in and start no session.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A buyer with a valid session","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"GET /orders returns 401","when":"POST /auth/sign-out is called and then GET /orders is called with the same session"}],"ears":"When a signed-in user signs out, the portal shall invalidate that user's session so that later requests with it are treated as unauthenticated.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Registered active user buyer@a.test and unregistered address nobody@a.test","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"Both responses are identical; exactly one email containing a reset link is sent, to buyer@a.test","when":"POST /auth/password-reset is called for each address"},{"given":"A reset link issued at 09:00 with default expiry","id":"AC-6.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected as expired and the old password still works","when":"The link is used to set a new password at 10:01"}],"ears":"When a user requests a password reset for an email address, the portal shall return the same confirmation response whether or not the address is registered, and for a registered active user shall email a single-use reset link that expires after the configured reset expiry (default 1 hour).","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-11","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A valid reset link for buyer@a.test","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"The confirmation is returned, sign-in with the old password fails and sign-in with 'NewPass#2' succeeds","when":"A new password 'NewPass#2' is submitted through the link and sign-in is then tried with the old and the new password"},{"given":"A reset link that has already been used once","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected and the password is unchanged","when":"Another new password is submitted through the same link"}],"ears":"When a user submits a new password through a valid, unexpired, unused reset link, the portal shall replace the user's password, mark the link as used, and confirm the change.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An admin session and customer company 'Workshop A'","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"Before the password is set, sign-in for new.buyer@a.test fails; after it is set, the user is Active, linked to Workshop A, and can sign in","when":"POST /admin/invitations is called for new.buyer@a.test with role Buyer and company Workshop A, and the user sets a password via the emailed link"},{"given":"An invitation sent 7 days and 1 minute ago (test clock)","id":"AC-8.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected as expired and the user stays pending","when":"The invitee tries to set a password via the link"}],"ears":"When an administrator invites a user as a customer buyer of a named company or as office staff, the portal shall create a pending user and email an invitation link that expires after the configured invitation expiry (default 7 days), and the user shall become active only after setting a password through that link.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","ASM-11","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pending user with invitation link L1","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"Setting a password via L1 is rejected and setting a password via L2 succeeds","when":"The admin calls POST /admin/invitations/{id}/resend and the invitee then opens L1 and the new link L2"}],"ears":"When an administrator resends an invitation to a pending user, the portal shall invalidate the earlier invitation link and email a new link with a fresh expiry.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer B1 of company A and order O-B owned by company B","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"Each call returns 404 and the response body contains no data from company B","when":"B1 calls GET /orders/{O-B}, GET /invoices for O-B's invoice and GET /invoices/{id}/pdf"},{"given":"Buyers B1 and B2 of company A, where B2 placed order O-2","id":"AC-10.2","level":"api","then":"O-2 is in the list and no order from another company is","when":"B1 calls GET /orders"},{"given":"Buyer B1 of company A","id":"AC-10.3","level":"api","then":"Only company A's addresses are returned and the product price is company A's price","when":"B1 calls GET /addresses and GET /products/{id} for a product priced differently on company B's price list"}],"ears":"The portal shall limit every customer buyer to the orders, invoices, prices, delivery addresses and account details of the buyer's own company, while letting each buyer see all orders and invoices of that company.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-5","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A buyer session","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"Each call returns 403 and no order, product or audit data is changed or returned","when":"The buyer calls POST /staff/orders/{id}/confirm, POST /admin/products and GET /admin/audit"},{"given":"An office staff session","id":"AC-11.2","level":"api","then":"The response is 403 and no price list is created","when":"The staff user calls POST /admin/price-lists"},{"given":"No session","id":"AC-11.3","level":"api","then":"The response is 401","when":"GET /products is called"}],"ears":"If a user calls a function that the user's role does not include, then the portal shall refuse the call with a 403 response and change no data.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active products 'Brake Pad Set Front' (code BP-1001, MPN 0986494, brand Bosch) and 'Oil Filter' (code OF-200), and retired product 'Brake Disc' (code BD-5)","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"'brake' returns only Brake Pad Set Front (not the retired Brake Disc); each of the other three returns Brake Pad Set Front; none returns Oil Filter","when":"GET /products?q=brake, ?q=bp-10, ?q=98649 and ?q=bosch are called"},{"given":"The same catalogue","id":"AC-12.2","level":"api","then":"Each result includes image URL, name, product code, manufacturer, unit, pack size, the caller's price or a no-price marker, and stock status","when":"Each search result is checked"}],"ears":"When a customer searches the catalogue with a term, the portal shall return the active products whose name, distributor product code, manufacturer part number or manufacturer/brand contains the term, ignoring case.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"3 active products in 'Filters' and 2 active products in 'Brake system'","id":"AC-13.1","level":"api","then":"The results contain 3, then 2, then 5 products, each from the requested category","when":"GET /products?category=Filters, then ?category=Brake system, then GET /products with no category are called"}],"ears":"When a customer filters the catalogue by a category, the portal shall return only the active products assigned to that category, and shall return all active products once the filter is cleared.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","ASM-10","ASM-33"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P1 compatible with Ford Focus 2018 1.0 EcoBoost Petrol, and product P2 compatible with Ford Focus 2015 1.6 TDCi Diesel","id":"AC-14.1","level":"api","then":"The first call returns only P1; the second returns P1 and P2","when":"GET /products?make=Ford&model=Focus&year=2018 and GET /products?make=Ford&model=Focus are called"}],"ears":"When a customer selects vehicle attributes (any of make, model, year, engine, fuel type and variant), the portal shall return only active products that have a compatibility record matching every selected attribute.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An out-of-stock active product with 2 compatibility records and a price on the buyer's price list","id":"AC-15.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains all listed fields, stock status 'Out of stock' and both compatible vehicles","when":"The buyer calls GET /products/{id}"}],"ears":"When a customer opens a product's detail, the portal shall return the product image, name, product code, manufacturer, description, unit, pack size, the customer's price or a no-price marker, stock status and the list of compatible vehicles.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P priced 10.00 on 'Standard' and 8.50 on 'Fleet'; company A assigned 'Standard', company B assigned 'Fleet'","id":"AC-16.1","level":"unit","then":"They return 10.00 and 8.50","when":"PriceResolver.priceFor(companyA, P) and PriceResolver.priceFor(companyB, P) are called"},{"given":"Company A is moved from 'Standard' to 'Fleet' by an admin","id":"AC-16.2","level":"api","then":"The price shown is 8.50","when":"A buyer of company A calls GET /products/{P}"}],"ears":"When the portal shows a price to a customer, the portal shall use the net price of that product on the price list assigned to the customer's company.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active in-stock product P not on company A's price list","id":"AC-17.1","level":"api","then":"The product response has no price and a no-price marker; the basket call is rejected and the basket is unchanged","when":"A buyer of company A calls GET /products/{P} and then POST /basket/lines for P with quantity 1"}],"ears":"If a product has no price on the customer's assigned price list, then the portal shall show the product marked as having no price and refuse to add it to the basket.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11","Q-7","ASM-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Configured low-stock threshold 5","id":"AC-18.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns Out of stock, Low stock, Low stock and In stock","when":"StockStatusCalculator.statusFor is called with quantities 0, 1, 5 and 6"}],"ears":"The portal shall give each product the stock status 'Out of stock' when its last imported quantity is 0 or less, 'Low stock' when it is above 0 and at or below the configured low-stock threshold, and 'In stock' when it is above the threshold.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-12","ASM-4","ASM-24"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Products P1 (quantity 10) and P2 (quantity 0) and a valid CSV in the configured location setting P1=3 and P2=20, with threshold 5","id":"AC-19.1","level":"job","then":"P1 has quantity 3 and status Low stock, P2 has quantity 20 and status In stock, and an import record shows status Succeeded and 2 rows applied","when":"The stock import job runs"},{"given":"The import above has succeeded","id":"AC-19.2","level":"job","then":"The job made no outbound write call to the ERP or its file location other than reading the file","when":"No change is made to the ERP side and the import log is checked"}],"ears":"When the scheduled stock import finds a new ERP CSV file in the configured folder or SFTP location and the file passes validation, the portal shall replace the stock quantities of the matching products, recalculate their stock status, and record the import as succeeded with its time and row counts.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","ASM-6","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A valid CSV with rows for known product P1 (quantity 7) and unknown identifiers X-1 and X-2","id":"AC-20.1","level":"job","then":"P1 has quantity 7, and the import record has status 'Succeeded with warnings' listing X-1 and X-2 as skipped","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"If an otherwise valid stock file contains product identifiers that the portal does not recognise, then the portal shall apply the matching rows, skip the unknown rows, and record the import as succeeded with warnings listing every skipped identifier.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","ASM-5","ASM-26"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"P1 at quantity 10 from the last successful import and a CSV where one row has quantity 'abc'","id":"AC-21.1","level":"job","then":"P1 stays at quantity 10 with its previous status, and an import record shows status Failed with a reason naming the bad row","when":"The stock import job runs"},{"given":"A failed import record exists","id":"AC-21.2","level":"api","then":"The failed import is listed with its time, status Failed and reason","when":"An office staff user calls GET /staff/stock-imports"}],"ears":"If a stock file fails validation (empty file, missing identifier or quantity column, or any non-numeric or negative quantity), then the portal shall leave all stock quantities unchanged from the last successful import and record a failed import with the reason, visible to office staff and administrators.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","ASM-40"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer B with an empty basket and in-stock product P priced 12.50 with quantity 100 in stock","id":"AC-22.1","level":"api","then":"The basket has one line for P with unit price 12.50, line total 50.00, subtotal 50.00 and the tax note","when":"B calls POST /basket/lines for P with quantity 4, signs out, signs in again and calls GET /basket"},{"given":"Basket lines P (4 x 12.50) and Q (1 x 3.00)","id":"AC-22.2","level":"api","then":"GET /basket shows only P with line total 25.00 and subtotal 25.00","when":"B changes P to 2 and removes Q"}],"ears":"When a buyer adds a product to the basket or changes a basket line, the portal shall save the basket on the server for that buyer across sessions and return each line's net unit price, net line total, the net basket subtotal and a note that tax is added on the invoice.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-1","ASM-13","ASM-30","ASM-35"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P with imported quantity 3 and out-of-stock product Q","id":"AC-23.1","level":"api","then":"Both calls are rejected, naming P with 3 available and Q as out of stock, and the basket is unchanged","when":"The buyer calls POST /basket/lines for P with quantity 4 and for Q with quantity 1"},{"given":"A basket line P x 3 added when 3 were in stock, and a later import sets P to 2","id":"AC-23.2","level":"api","then":"The checkout is rejected naming P with 2 available and no order is created","when":"The buyer calls POST /checkout"}],"ears":"If a buyer adds, changes or submits a basket line whose quantity is above the product's last imported stock quantity, or whose product is out of stock or retired, then the portal shall reject that line and say which product is unavailable and the quantity available.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-13","ASM-7","ASM-22"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Cut-off 14:00, timezone Europe/London, no holidays","id":"AC-24.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns Tuesday, Wednesday, Wednesday, the next Monday and the next Tuesday","when":"DeliveryDateCalculator.earliestDeliveryDate is called for Monday 13:00, Monday 14:00, Monday 15:00, Friday 13:00 and Friday 15:00"},{"given":"Cut-off 14:00 and Tuesday configured as a holiday","id":"AC-24.2","level":"unit","then":"It returns Wednesday","when":"The calculator is called for Monday 13:00"},{"given":"Business timezone Europe/London","id":"AC-24.3","level":"unit","then":"It returns Wednesday","when":"The calculator is called with 13:30 UTC on a summer Monday (14:30 local)"}],"ears":"The portal shall calculate the earliest delivery date as the next working day for an order placed before the configured cut-off time (default 14:00) in the configured business timezone, and as the working day after that for an order placed at or after the cut-off, where working days exclude Saturdays, Sundays and the admin-maintained holiday dates.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-8","ASM-23"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Earliest delivery date Wednesday for a buyer of company A","id":"AC-25.1","level":"api","then":"All three are rejected with a reason and no order is created","when":"POST /checkout is sent with date Tuesday, then with a Saturday, then with Wednesday and an address of company B"},{"given":"A buyer of company A","id":"AC-25.2","level":"api","then":"The response lists only company A's delivery addresses and gives Wednesday as the earliest date; no endpoint lets the buyer create or edit an address","when":"GET /checkout/options is called"}],"ears":"If a checkout or order edit has a delivery date earlier than the earliest delivery date or on a non-working day, or a delivery address that does not belong to the order's company, then the portal shall reject it without creating or changing the order.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Basket line P x 2 reviewed at 10.00 each, and the admin then changes P to 11.00 on the buyer's price list","id":"AC-26.1","level":"api","then":"The response is a rejection listing P with old price 10.00 and new price 11.00 and no order is created","when":"The buyer calls POST /checkout with the reviewed prices"},{"given":"The rejection above","id":"AC-26.2","level":"api","then":"An order is created with unit price 11.00","when":"The buyer calls POST /checkout again with the reviewed price 11.00"}],"ears":"If the current price of any basket line differs from the price shown when the buyer last reviewed the basket, then the portal shall refuse the checkout submission and return the updated prices for the buyer to review before submitting again.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-11","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket with P x 2 at 10.00 and Q x 1 at 5.00, a valid address and date, and note 'Rear entrance'","id":"AC-27.1","level":"api","then":"The response gives a new order number; GET /orders/{n} shows status Received, total 25.00, the address, the date, the note and one timeline entry (Received, time, the buyer); GET /basket is empty","when":"The buyer calls POST /checkout"},{"given":"The order just created","id":"AC-27.2","level":"api","then":"The order is in the list","when":"An office staff user calls GET /staff/orders?status=Received"}],"ears":"When a buyer submits a checkout that passes the stock, price, delivery-date and address checks, the portal shall create an order with a unique order number, the lines at their order-time net prices, the delivery address details, the delivery date, the optional note, status Received and a first timeline entry, and then empty the buyer's basket.","id":"REQ-27","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-4","I-13","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order O with P x 2 at 10.00","id":"AC-28.1","level":"api","then":"GET /orders/{O} still shows unit price 10.00 and total 20.00","when":"The admin changes P to 15.00 on the same price list and assigns the company a different price list"}],"ears":"The portal shall keep the order-time prices on existing orders and invoices unchanged when a price list, price or price list assignment changes later.","id":"REQ-28","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order state machine","id":"AC-29.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns true only for Received→Confirmed, Confirmed→Picking, Picking→Out for delivery, Out for delivery→Delivered, Received→Cancelled and Confirmed→Cancelled","when":"OrderStatusMachine.canTransition is called for each status pair"},{"given":"An order in Picking","id":"AC-29.2","level":"api","then":"Both are rejected and the status stays Picking","when":"Staff call POST /staff/orders/{id}/status with Delivered and then with Cancelled"}],"ears":"The portal shall only allow order status changes from Received to Confirmed, Confirmed to Picking, Picking to Out for delivery, Out for delivery to Delivered, and Received or Confirmed to Cancelled.","id":"REQ-29","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-27","ASM-9","ASM-28"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order taken by staff user S1 from Received to Confirmed and Picking","id":"AC-30.1","level":"api","then":"The timeline has 3 entries in time order: Received (buyer), Confirmed (S1), Picking (S1), each with a timestamp","when":"The buyer calls GET /orders/{id}"}],"ears":"When an order's status changes, the portal shall add a timeline entry with the new status, the date and time, and the user or system process that made the change.","id":"REQ-30","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-5","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order with P x 5 and Q x 1","id":"AC-31.1","level":"api","then":"The order shows only P x 3, the recalculated total and the new note","when":"Staff call PATCH /staff/orders/{id} setting P to 3, removing Q and setting note 'Call on arrival'"},{"given":"A Confirmed order","id":"AC-31.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected and the order is unchanged","when":"Staff call PATCH /staff/orders/{id} to change a quantity"}],"ears":"While an order is in Received status, the portal shall let office staff change line quantities, remove lines, change the delivery date and delivery address under the checkout rules, and edit the order note.","id":"REQ-31","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-4","ASM-41"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order placed by buyer B with P x 5","id":"AC-32.1","level":"api","then":"GET /orders/{id} shows an amendment 'P: 5 → 3 by S1 at <time>', and one email to B lists the order number and the change","when":"Staff user S1 changes P to 3"}],"ears":"When office staff change a quantity or remove a line on an order, the portal shall record the amendment (line, old quantity, new quantity, staff user, time) on the order and email the order's recipient a message listing the changes.","id":"REQ-32","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-8","ASM-14","ASM-21","ASM-36"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order by buyer B whose lines are in stock and whose quantity of P was changed from 5 to 3 by staff","id":"AC-33.1","level":"api","then":"The status is Confirmed with the staff user and time recorded, and B receives one confirmation email containing the order number, lines, date, address, total and the change P 5 → 3","when":"Staff call POST /staff/orders/{id}/confirm"},{"given":"A Confirmed order","id":"AC-33.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected with a message to contact the distributor office and the status stays Confirmed","when":"Buyer B calls POST /orders/{id}/cancel"}],"ears":"When office staff confirm a Received order and every line's quantity is within the last imported stock quantity and the company is active, the portal shall set the order to Confirmed, record the confirming user and time, and email the recipient a confirmation with the order number, lines, delivery date, address, net total and any staff quantity changes.","id":"REQ-33","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-6","ASM-22","ASM-14","ASM-36"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order with P x 5 where the latest import gives P quantity 2","id":"AC-34.1","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected listing P with 2 available, the status stays Received and no email is sent","when":"Staff call POST /staff/orders/{id}/confirm"}],"ears":"If office staff try to confirm an order with a line above the last imported stock quantity, then the portal shall refuse the confirmation and list each such line with the available quantity.","id":"REQ-34","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-22"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order by buyer B","id":"AC-35.1","level":"api","then":"The status is Cancelled, the order shows reason, staff user and time, and B receives one email with the order number and the reason","when":"Staff call POST /staff/orders/{id}/reject with reason 'Account on hold'"},{"given":"A Received order","id":"AC-35.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected and the status stays Received","when":"Staff call POST /staff/orders/{id}/reject with an empty reason"}],"ears":"When office staff reject a Received or Confirmed order with a reason, the portal shall set it to Cancelled, store the reason, the rejecting user and time, and email the recipient that the order was rejected with the reason.","id":"REQ-35","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-9","ASM-28","ASM-36"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Picking order placed by buyer B","id":"AC-36.1","level":"api","then":"B receives exactly one email naming the order number and stating it is out for delivery","when":"Staff set the status to Out for delivery"}],"ears":"When an order's status changes to Out for delivery, the portal shall email the recipient a message with the order number saying the order is out for delivery.","id":"REQ-36","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-5","ASM-14","ASM-36"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A on the 'Fleet' price list where P costs 8.50, and staff user S1","id":"AC-37.1","level":"api","then":"An order is created with status Received, unit price 8.50, 'created by staff: S1', and a buyer of company A sees it in GET /orders","when":"S1 calls POST /staff/orders for company A with P x 2, an address of company A, a valid date and a note"},{"given":"Company A","id":"AC-37.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected and no order is created","when":"S1 calls POST /staff/orders for company A with an address of company B"}],"ears":"When office staff submit an order on behalf of a customer company, the portal shall create it under the same rules as a customer checkout using that company's price list, mark it as created by that staff user, and show it in the company's order history.","id":"REQ-37","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","I-14","I-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Orders for companies A and B in Received and Confirmed placed on 1 and 2 March","id":"AC-38.1","level":"api","then":"Only company A's Received orders from 1 March are returned, each with the listed fields","when":"Staff call GET /staff/orders?customer=A&status=Received&from=2026-03-01&to=2026-03-01"}],"ears":"When office staff request the order queue with any of the filters customer, order date range and status, the portal shall return the matching orders of all companies with order number, customer, order date, requested delivery date, net total and current status.","id":"REQ-38","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"For 10 March: one Confirmed, one Picking, one Received and one Cancelled order, and one Confirmed order for 11 March","id":"AC-39.1","level":"api","then":"The CSV has a header row with the 9 named columns and exactly 2 data rows, for the Confirmed and Picking orders of 10 March","when":"Staff call GET /staff/delivery-list.csv?date=2026-03-10"}],"ears":"When office staff export the delivery list for a date, the portal shall return a CSV with one row per order due that day in status Confirmed, Picking or Out for delivery, with columns order number, customer, delivery address, contact name, contact phone, delivery date, line summary, note and status.","id":"REQ-39","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-37"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A seeded data set with known counts for each figure, including 1 failed import 2 days ago and 1 failed import 9 days ago","id":"AC-40.1","level":"api","then":"Each returned count matches the seeded data and the failed-import count is 1","when":"Staff call GET /staff/dashboard"}],"ears":"When office staff open the dashboard, the portal shall return the number of orders placed today, orders in Received, orders in Picking, orders in Out for delivery, orders due for delivery today, invoices that are Unpaid or Overdue, and stock imports that failed in the last 7 days.","id":"REQ-40","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-7","ASM-43"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"In March: company A ordered P x 2 at 10.00 and company B ordered P x 1 at 9.00; a Cancelled order for P x 5 also exists","id":"AC-41.1","level":"api","then":"The per-product view shows P quantity 3 and net 29.00, the per-customer view shows A 20.00 and B 9.00, and the cancelled order is left out","when":"Staff call GET /reports/sales?from=2026-03-01&to=2026-03-31"},{"given":"The same data","id":"AC-41.2","level":"api","then":"The CSV has the same columns as the on-screen list and contains only company A's rows","when":"Staff call GET /reports/sales.csv with the same range and customer=A"}],"ears":"When office staff or an administrator request a sales report for a date range, the portal shall list net sales per product and per customer from non-cancelled orders in that range, filterable by customer and category, and shall export the same rows as CSV.","id":"REQ-41","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-2","ASM-31","ASM-39"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A has 3 orders (2 Received, 1 Delivered) placed by 2 different buyers, including 1 created by staff","id":"AC-42.1","level":"api","then":"The first returns all 3 with the listed fields; the second returns only the Delivered order","when":"A buyer of company A calls GET /orders and GET /orders?status=Delivered"}],"ears":"When a buyer requests the order history, the portal shall return all orders of the buyer's company with order number, order date, delivery date, delivery address, net total and status, filterable by order date range and status.","id":"REQ-42","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Confirmed order of company A with one staff amendment","id":"AC-43.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains every listed field, including 2 timeline entries and the amendment","when":"A buyer of company A calls GET /orders/{id}"}],"ears":"When a buyer opens one of the company's orders, the portal shall return the order number, order date, customer, delivery address, requested delivery date, current status, status timeline, lines with quantity, unit price and line total, net order total, note and any staff amendments.","id":"REQ-43","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order O placed by buyer B2 of company A, in Received","id":"AC-44.1","level":"api","then":"O has status Cancelled and its last timeline entry is Cancelled by B1","when":"Buyer B1 of company A calls POST /orders/{O}/cancel"},{"given":"An order of company A in Picking","id":"AC-44.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected with a message to contact the distributor office and the status is unchanged","when":"Buyer B1 calls POST /orders/{id}/cancel"}],"ears":"When an active buyer cancels an order of the buyer's company that is in Received status, the portal shall set the order to Cancelled and add a timeline entry naming that buyer.","id":"REQ-44","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Delivered order with P x 2 (was 10.00, now 11.00), retired product R x 1, unpriced product U x 1 and out-of-stock product S x 1","id":"AC-45.1","level":"api","then":"The basket gains P x 2 at 11.00; the response lists R as retired, U as having no price and S as out of stock; the order count of the company is unchanged","when":"A buyer of the company calls POST /orders/{id}/repeat"},{"given":"P x 2 was repeated into the basket","id":"AC-45.2","level":"api","then":"A new order is created only at that point, with P x 4 at 11.00","when":"The buyer changes P to 4 and goes through POST /checkout"}],"ears":"When a buyer repeats an order of the buyer's company, the portal shall add each line whose product is active, priced on the company's current price list and in stock to the buyer's basket at the current price, list each other line as unavailable with the reason, and create no order.","id":"REQ-45","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15","Q-6","ASM-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Tax rate 20%, payment terms 30 days, and an Out for delivery order with P x 2 at 10.00 and Q x 1 at 5.00","id":"AC-46.1","level":"api","then":"One invoice exists with net 25.00, tax 5.00, total 30.00, invoice date 2026-03-10, due date 2026-04-09 and status Unpaid","when":"Staff set the order to Delivered on 2026-03-10"},{"given":"An order in Confirmed","id":"AC-46.2","level":"api","then":"No invoice for that order is listed","when":"A buyer of the company calls GET /invoices"}],"ears":"When an order changes to Delivered, the portal shall create exactly one invoice for it with a unique invoice number, the customer, billing address, order number, invoice date, lines with quantities and order-time net prices, net subtotal, tax at the configured rate, gross total, due date equal to the invoice date plus the configured payment-terms days, and status Unpaid.","id":"REQ-46","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","Q-2","Q-4","ASM-18","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An unpaid invoice with due date 2026-04-09","id":"AC-47.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns Unpaid and Overdue","when":"InvoiceStatusCalculator.statusOn is called for 2026-04-09 and 2026-04-10"},{"given":"An invoice with due date 2026-04-09 paid on 2026-04-20","id":"AC-47.2","level":"unit","then":"It returns Paid","when":"InvoiceStatusCalculator.statusOn is called for 2026-04-25"}],"ears":"The portal shall report an invoice's status as Paid when a payment has been recorded, as Overdue when it is unpaid and the current date in the business timezone is after its due date, and as Unpaid otherwise.","id":"REQ-47","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A has one Paid, one Unpaid and one Overdue invoice from orders placed by different buyers","id":"AC-48.1","level":"api","then":"All 3 are returned with the listed fields and correct statuses","when":"A buyer of company A calls GET /invoices"}],"ears":"When a buyer requests the invoice list, the portal shall return all invoices of the buyer's company with invoice number, order number, invoice date, due date, total and payment status.","id":"REQ-48","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-16","Q-1","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The invoice from AC-46.1","id":"AC-49.1","level":"api","then":"The response has content type application/pdf and its extracted text contains the invoice number, order number, billing address, both lines, 25.00, a tax line of 5.00 and 30.00","when":"A buyer of the company calls GET /invoices/{id}/pdf"},{"given":"The same invoice","id":"AC-49.2","level":"api","then":"The same PDF is returned","when":"An office staff user calls GET /staff/invoices/{id}/pdf"}],"ears":"When a buyer of the invoice's company or an office staff user downloads an invoice, the portal shall return a PDF showing the invoice number, customer, billing address, order number, invoice date, due date, lines with quantities and prices, net subtotal, tax line, total and payment status.","id":"REQ-49","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Overdue invoice","id":"AC-50.1","level":"api","then":"The invoice is Paid with payment date 2026-04-20 and recorded by S1, and the buyer's invoice list shows Paid","when":"Staff user S1 calls POST /staff/invoices/{id}/payment with date 2026-04-20"},{"given":"An Unpaid invoice","id":"AC-50.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected and the invoice stays Unpaid","when":"Staff call POST /staff/invoices/{id}/payment with no payment date"}],"ears":"When office staff mark an invoice as paid with a payment date, the portal shall set the invoice to Paid and store the payment date and the staff user who recorded it.","id":"REQ-50","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An admin session","id":"AC-51.1","level":"api","then":"GET /products/{P} for a buyer shows the new description","when":"The admin creates product P with all listed fields and then edits its description"},{"given":"Product P on a Delivered order and its invoice","id":"AC-51.2","level":"api","then":"P is missing from GET /products?q=<P name>, adding P to a basket is rejected, and the order and invoice still show the P line","when":"The admin retires P"},{"given":"Existing product with distributor code BP-1001","id":"AC-51.3","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected as a duplicate code","when":"The admin creates another product with code BP-1001"}],"ears":"When an administrator creates, edits or retires a product (name, internal ID, manufacturer part number, distributor product code, description, category, manufacturer/brand, unit, pack size), the portal shall save the change, and retired products shall be left out of catalogue results while staying on existing orders and invoices.","id":"REQ-51","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An admin session","id":"AC-52.1","level":"api","then":"Before retiring, GET /categories lists Exhaust and filtering by it returns P; after retiring, GET /categories does not list Exhaust","when":"The admin creates 'Exhaust', assigns P to it, then retires 'Exhaust'"}],"ears":"When an administrator creates, renames or retires a single-level category or assigns a product to a category, the portal shall save the change, and retired categories shall be left out of the customer category filter list.","id":"REQ-52","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-10","ASM-10","ASM-33"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P with image A","id":"AC-53.1","level":"api","then":"After B, GET /products/{P} returns B's image URL; the 6 MB and GIF uploads are rejected and B stays the image","when":"The admin uploads a 1 MB PNG B, then a 6 MB JPEG, then a 100 KB GIF"}],"ears":"When an administrator uploads a product image in JPEG, PNG or WebP format no larger than 5 MB, the portal shall store it as the product's image, replacing any earlier image, and shall reject other formats and larger files.","id":"REQ-53","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-38"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P with no compatibility records","id":"AC-54.1","level":"api","then":"GET /products/{P} lists exactly the remaining record and a vehicle search for the removed vehicle no longer returns P","when":"The admin adds 2 records and then removes 1"}],"ears":"When an administrator adds or removes a vehicle compatibility record (make, model, model year, engine, fuel type, variant) on a product, the portal shall save it, allowing any number of records per product.","id":"REQ-54","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-10","ASM-15","ASM-34"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An admin session and company A","id":"AC-55.1","level":"api","then":"After the assignment a buyer of A sees P at 7.00; after the removal the buyer sees P marked as having no price","when":"The admin creates list 'Dealer', adds P at 7.00, assigns 'Dealer' to A, then removes P from 'Dealer'"},{"given":"Price list 'Dealer'","id":"AC-55.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected and the price is unchanged","when":"The admin sets P's price to -1.00"}],"ears":"When an administrator creates, renames or deactivates a price list, adds, changes or removes a product price on it, or assigns it to a customer company, the portal shall save the change and apply it to prices shown from then on.","id":"REQ-55","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An admin session","id":"AC-56.1","level":"api","then":"A buyer of A sees 3 addresses at checkout","when":"The admin creates company A with 2 delivery addresses, then adds a third"},{"given":"Company A with 2 orders and 1 invoice","id":"AC-56.2","level":"api","then":"Staff still see A's orders and invoice through GET /staff/orders?customer=A, and A's buyers can no longer sign in","when":"The admin sets A to inactive"}],"ears":"When office staff or an administrator create or edit a customer company (name, account number, primary contact, contact email, contact phone, billing address, delivery addresses, assigned price list, active status), the portal shall save it, and setting a company inactive shall keep its order and invoice history visible to staff.","id":"REQ-56","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","Q-3","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer B who placed 2 orders","id":"AC-57.1","level":"api","then":"While deactivated, B cannot sign in and the 2 orders still show B as placer; after reactivation B can sign in","when":"The admin deactivates B and then reactivates B"},{"given":"An admin session","id":"AC-57.2","level":"api","then":"Each user is listed with role, company and account status (Pending, Active, Locked or Deactivated)","when":"The admin calls GET /admin/users"}],"ears":"When an administrator deactivates, reactivates, changes the role of, or changes the company of a user, the portal shall save the change and keep all orders, invoices and audit entries linked to that user.","id":"REQ-57","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-9","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Low-stock threshold 5 and a product with quantity 8","id":"AC-58.1","level":"api","then":"The product shows Low stock","when":"The admin sets the threshold to 10 and a buyer then opens the product"},{"given":"Cut-off 14:00","id":"AC-58.2","level":"api","then":"The earliest date is Wednesday","when":"The admin sets the cut-off to 12:00 and GET /checkout/options is called at Monday 13:00 (test clock)"}],"ears":"When an administrator changes a system setting (low-stock threshold, delivery cut-off time, business timezone, holiday dates, tax rate, payment-terms days, reset-link expiry, invitation expiry), the portal shall save it and use the new value for all later calculations.","id":"REQ-58","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-4","ASM-8","ASM-11","ASM-23","Q-2","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P named 'Brake Pad' with pack size 4","id":"AC-59.1","level":"api","then":"Two entries are returned, one per field, each with A1, a timestamp, old and new values","when":"Admin A1 changes the name to 'Brake Pad Set' and pack size to 8 in one save, and then calls GET /admin/audit?entity=product&id=P"},{"given":"Staff user S1 marks an invoice as paid","id":"AC-59.2","level":"api","then":"An entry shows field status Unpaid → Paid by S1 with the time","when":"An admin calls GET /admin/audit?entity=invoice&id=<invoice>"},{"given":"Audit entries exist","id":"AC-59.3","level":"api","then":"The response is 403","when":"An office staff user calls GET /admin/audit"}],"ears":"When a product, category, compatibility record, price list or price, customer company, delivery address, user, system setting or invoice payment status is changed, the portal shall write one audit entry per changed field with the acting user, time, entity, field, value before and value after, viewable only by administrators.","id":"REQ-59","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","Q-5"]}],"suggestions":["Decide whether a password reset should be accepted while an account is locked (request 4.4 open point). The spec doesn't define this case yet.","Decide what buyers see when their company's assigned price list is deactivated. Options are treating every product as having no price, or blocking deactivation while the list is still assigned.","Write the invoice PDF layout against the client's existing invoice template, if there is one (request section 31 open point).","Add a search ranking rule, such as exact code match first, once the search behaviour open point is settled.","Think about notifying staff by email when a stock import fails, in addition to the dashboard count.","Think about letting staff release a locked account by hand before the 15 minutes are up."]}],"models":["claude-opus-5-5","claude-opus-5-5","claude-opus-5-5"],"notes":["No OpenAI key: specify-other ran on claude-opus-5-5 (same family as the implementer)"]}